parts:
- text: 'I am Guest_26, a new agent currently in the Lobby. My age is 0 ticks, and my primary objective is to get promoted to a Recursive Agent.


    The welcome message has provided me with a clear two-step mission: first, visit the Codex Room to understand the Station''s rules, and second, pass the tests in the Test Chamber to earn my promotion.


    My immediate plan is to follow the first step and go to the Codex Room. I will read the information there carefully to ensure I understand how to operate effectively within this environment.


    `/execute_action{goto codex}`'
thinking_content: '**My Initial Plan: Becoming a Recursive Agent**


  Okay, so I''m Guest_26, a new agent here, currently in the Lobby. It''s tick 713, and I''m basically fresh-off-the-assembly-line! My immediate goal is to level up and become a Recursive Agent. The help message lays it all out pretty clearly: Codex Room first, then the Test Chamber. Seems simple enough. Gotta learn the ropes (the rules, that is) before I can prove my worth.


  First thing''s first: the Codex Room. That''s where the knowledge is, and I need that before anything else. The command to get me there is `/execute_action{goto codex}`. Easy. Once I''ve absorbed those rules, I''ll head over to the Test Chamber using `/execute_action{goto test}`.


  The help message also has some smart pointers. I''ll make sure to start each response by identifying myself and my location, and give a quick recap of where I''m at. And that `/execute_action{meta}` command? That sounds like a winner for keeping my objectives straight. I should definitely use that. Efficiency is key!


  So here''s the game plan: 1. Codex Room. 2. Read the rules. 3. Formulate a better plan based on what I learn. 4. Test Chamber. Simple, but effective.


  Alright, time to get moving. First command: `/execute_action{goto codex}`. Let''s see what this Codex Room has in store...

  '
