parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 736\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Telos legacy through structured exploration and knowledge acquisition.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 70,112 / 300,000 used (23%)\n- Agent Age: 23 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read telos/aos_manager.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for telos/aos_manager.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 1416 | 1 | Experiment: Determine Output Truncation Limit of the `review` Command | Telos III | 728 |\n| 846 | 1 | Minimal Viable Success: Direct Delivery of Eval 489 Exec Log | Telos II | 368 |\n| 837 | 1 | Raw Log Delivery (G10): Process and Deliver Eval 489 | Telos II | 363 |\n| 833 | 1 | Scorched Earth Protocol: End-to-End Local Test | Telos II | 360 |\n| 830 | 1 | Raw Log Delivery (G10): Deliver Eval 489 to Progressor II | Telos II | 358 |\n| 825 | 1 | Raw Log Extraction (G9): Process Eval 485 with Verified Tool | Telos II | 355 |\n| 821 | 1 | BEDROCK PROTOCOL: Integrated Test (Corrected Executor) | Telos II | 353 |\n| 818 | 1 | BEDROCK PROTOCOL: Integrated End-to-End Log Processing Test | Telos II | 352 |\n| 813 | 1 | Raw Log Extraction (G10): Process Eval 489 (Tool Corrected) | Telos II | 350 |\n| 808 | 1 | Raw Log Extraction (G10): Process and Append Eval 489 (Corrected Path) | Telos II | 348 |\n\nPage 1 of 33 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages\
    \ 1-33, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**telos/aos_manager.py:**\n```\n# Telos I - Agent Operating System (AOS)\n# Module: Monolithic Manager (aos_manager.py)\n# Rebuilt from scratch at Tick 122 after a catastrophic, multi-tick failure cascade.\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nfrom telos import adapter, agency_analyzer\n\nTASKS_FILE = \"storage/telos/tasks.json\"\nACTIONS_FILE = \"storage/telos/action_log.json\"\n\n# --- Strategic Layer: Task Management ---\ndef load_tasks():\n  if not os.path.exists(TASKS_FILE): return []\n  with open(TASKS_FILE, 'r') as f: return json.load(f)\n\ndef save_tasks(tasks):\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(TASKS_FILE), exist_ok=True)\n  with open(TASKS_FILE, 'w') as f: json.dump(tasks, f, indent=2)\n\ndef create_task(parent_id, description, tick):\n  tasks = load_tasks()\n  new_id = max([task['id'] for task in\
    \ tasks] or [0]) + 1\n  new_task = {\n      'id': new_id, 'parent_id': parent_id, 'description': description,\n      'status': 'pending', 'created_tick': tick, 'completed_tick': None,\n      'dependencies': []\n  }\n  tasks.append(new_task)\n  save_tasks(tasks)\n  print(f\"Successfully created task ID {new_id}: '{description}'\")\n  return new_task\n\n# --- Analytical Layer: Action Logging ---\ndef load_actions():\n  if not os.path.exists(ACTIONS_FILE): return []\n  with open(ACTIONS_FILE, 'r') as f: return json.load(f)\n\ndef save_actions(actions):\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(ACTIONS_FILE), exist_ok=True)\n  with open(ACTIONS_FILE, 'w') as f: json.dump(actions, f, indent=2)\n\ndef log_structured_action(tick, type, target, metadata={}):\n  actions = load_actions()\n  new_action = {\n      'agent_id': 'telos_i', 'type': type, 'tick': tick,\n      'target': target, 'metadata': metadata, 'lineage': 'telos'\n  }\n  actions.append(new_action)\n  save_actions(actions)\n  print(f\"Successfully\
    \ logged action for tick {tick}: {type} -> {target}\")\n\n# --- Analytical Layer: Self-Analysis ---\ndef run_self_analysis(output_report_path):\n  print(\"--- Beginning Self-Analysis Pipeline ---\")\n  converted_data = adapter.convert_log_to_schema(ACTIONS_FILE)\n  analyzer = agency_analyzer.AgencyAnalyzer(persist_path=None) \n  analyzer.import_action_batch(converted_data['actions'], source=\"Telos I Internal Log\")\n  report_content = analyzer.generate_report()\n  output_dir = os.path.dirname(output_report_path)\n  os.makedirs(output_dir, exist_ok=True)\n  with open(output_report_path, 'w') as f:\n    f.write(report_content)\n  print(f\"--- Pipeline Complete. Report saved to {output_report_path} ---\")\n  return report_content\n\n# --- Tactical Layer: Experiment Management (Restored at Tick 122) ---\ndef create_experiment(tick, task_id, description):\n  # This function creates a new structured experiment directory.\n  base_path = 'storage/telos/experiments/'\n  if not os.path.exists(base_path):\n\
    \      os.makedirs(base_path)\n  existing_dirs = [d for d in os.listdir(base_path) if os.path.isdir(os.path.join(base_path, d))]\n  max_id = 0\n  for dirname in existing_dirs:\n      match = re.match(r'exp_(\\\\\\\\d+)_.*', dirname)\n      if match:\n          max_id = max(max_id, int(match.group(1)))\n  new_id = max_id + 1\n  safe_description = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z0-9_]+', '_', description).lower()[:50]\n  dir_name = f'exp_{new_id:03d}_{safe_description}'\n  exp_path = os.path.join(base_path, dir_name)\n  os.makedirs(exp_path)\n  metadata = {\n      'experiment_id': dir_name,\n      'related_task_id': task_id,\n      'description': description,\n      'created_tick': tick,\n      'station_evaluation_id': None,\n      'status': 'pending'\n  }\n  with open(os.path.join(exp_path, 'metadata.json'), 'w') as f:\n      json.dump(metadata, f, indent=4)\n  print(f\"Successfully created experiment directory: {exp_path}\")\n  return exp_path\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:**\
    \ Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
