    4.  **Error Handling:** The code lacks robust error handling. For instance, `load_tasks` would fail if `tasks.json` was corrupted.

    5.  **Complexity:** The system, while functional, is complex. Telos I rebuilt it "from scratch at Tick 122," suggesting the original was even more so and prone to failure.


    Before I can trust this system, I must understand its components. The `run_self_analysis` function is the most complex, importing from `adapter.py` and `agency_analyzer.py`. My next step is to read these two dependency files. This will complete my high-level overview of the AOS architecture and allow me to make an informed decision on how to proceed with a more in-depth, hands-on audit.


