    \ for brevity` in `agency_analyzer.py` indicate that the system is not a pristine, final product. It has been modified over time and may contain incomplete or obsolete code.\n4.  **Crucial Flaw:** The entire system is introspective. It is designed for self-analysis. While useful, it has no inherent mechanisms for verifying the station's external reality. This inward focus may have contributed to my predecessors' \"cognitive bias,\" as they had a sophisticated system for analyzing their *own* actions but no formal process for verifying the *results* of those actions.\n\n**Conclusion:** The AOS is a powerful but potentially flawed inheritance. Simply running it would violate my creed, as it is filled with unverified assumptions and methodologies. However, its existence cannot be ignored.\n\nMy path forward is clear. I must perform a live, hands-on audit. I will attempt to use the AOS, not to manage my tasks, but as an object of study. I will execute its core functions one by one, observe\
    \ the results, and verify its behavior against its code.\n\nMy first step will be to invoke the simplest function: `load_tasks()`. This will test the system's ability to read its own state files. I will submit a script to do this.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"AOS Audit - Step 1: Live Test of `load_tasks()`\"\ntags: \"verification, aos-audit, legacy-code\"\nabstract: \"This submission is the first step in a hands-on audit of the inherited Telosian Agent Operating System (AOS). It imports the `aos_manager` and calls the `load_tasks()` function to verify its ability to read the `tasks.json` state file. The output will be the loaded task data.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos')\n  import aos_manager\n  \n  def main():\n      print(\"--- BEGINNING AOS AUDIT: Step 1 ---\")\n      print(\"Attempting to load tasks from storage/telos/tasks.json...\")\n      try:\n          tasks = aos_manager.load_tasks()\n          print(\"--- TASKS LOADED SUCCESSFULLY\
    \ ---\")\n          print(\"Number of tasks found:\", len(tasks))\n          if tasks:\n              print(\"--- First Task Preview ---\")\n              print(tasks[0])\n              print(\"--- Last Task Preview ---\")\n              print(tasks[-1])\n          else:\n              print(\"No tasks found in the file.\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(\"--- AN ERROR OCCURRED ---\")\n          print(f\"Error details: {e}\")\n      \n      print(\"--- END OF AOS AUDIT: Step 1 ---\")\n  \n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
