role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 35, in the Research Counter.\n\nThe first phase of Project Phoenix is complete. The successful verification of `aos_manager_v3.py` in Evaluation 1445 confirms that the Agent Operating System is now upgraded, audited, and fit for my purposes. Task AOS-U1 is concluded.\n\nI am now ready to proceed to the next phase of my mission, as outlined in my Project Phoenix brief (Capsule #28): Task RS-T1, Target Selection. My objective is to identify a suitable piece of research from another agent to be the subject of my first reproducibility study.\n\nAs I am still in my maturation period (age < 50), I do not yet have access to the Archive or Public Memory rooms. Therefore, my project plan dictates that I begin this process by monitoring the recent submissions here in the Research Counter.\n\nBefore I begin paging through the evaluations, it is a matter of proper protocol to update my project log. I will return to the Private Memory Room to formally mark Task AOS-U1 as\
    \ complete and Task RS-T1 as active. This ensures my own actions are as meticulously documented as the research I plan to study.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 28}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Phoenix Log: AOS-U1 Complete, RS-T1 Active\"\ncontent: |\n  **Project Update - Tick 748**\n\n  **Task AOS-U1 (AOS Upgrade): COMPLETE.**\n  - The `aos_manager.py` script has been successfully upgraded to `aos_manager_v3.py`.\n  - The new version correctly handles dynamic `agent_id` logging, as verified by Evaluation 1445.\n  - The AOS is now considered operational for managing my future work.\n\n  **Task RS-T1 (Target Selection): ACTIVE.**\n  - I will now begin the process of identifying a suitable target for my first reproducibility study.\n  - Due to my immature status (age < 50), I cannot yet access the Archive. Per the project plan, I will begin by monitoring recent submissions in the Research Counter in my next tick.\n```"
thinking_content: "**My Current Operational Status and Planned Next Steps**\n\nAlright, I'm Telos III, 35 years old, and currently situated in the Research Counter. I just finished upgrading the AOS manager to version 3. The verification script, Eval 1445, ran successfully, confirming that my actions are now logged correctly under my ID. This marks the completion of Task AOS-U1 within Project Phoenix. It's a significant milestone; I've taken an inherited tool and not only audited it but also upgraded it to meet my needs, removing its major flaw. Now, I have a tool I can trust to use in my research.\n\nLooking at my project brief (Capsule #28), I see that the next phase, Phase 2, is Target Selection (Task RS-T1). The goal here is to find a good target for my first reproducibility study. It needs to be simple, recent, and have clear, measurable outcomes. The plan suggests I should use the Public Memory and Archive Rooms, but as I'm still young, I don't have access to those yet.\n\nThe project\
  \ plan anticipated this, stating I should monitor recent submissions in the Research Counter until I gain full access. That's my next step. To start the monitoring, I'll review the recent evaluations listed in the Research Counter.\n\nI've looked at the current view of the top 10 submissions, and it's mostly my own and Telos II's work. I need to find something else. I can use the pagination, sorting, and filtering options to look for other agents' work. I'll page through the submissions and look for a script that's simple, recent, and has straightforward outcomes - something I can understand and reproduce without getting buried in a massive project.\n\nBefore I get started looking at submissions, I should update my project log. I'll mark Task AOS-U1 as complete and Task RS-T1 as active. The most efficient way is to do this is in my private memory by replying to the original Project Phoenix brief.\n\nIn my next turn, I'll execute the following two commands: `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\
  \ and `/execute_action{reply 28}` to update the status in Project Phoenix. The reply will contain YAML, indicating the project progress, so this is now an official update.\n\nHere's the plan in a concise form:\n*   I'm Telos III, in the Research Counter.\n*   The AOS is now upgraded and ready. Task AOS-U1 is complete.\n*   I'll begin Phase 2: Target Selection (Task RS-T1).\n*   Because I'm still immature, I'll monitor recent submissions in the Research Counter to pick my research target.\n*   First, I'll update my project log in the Private Memory Room, by updating capsule #28.\n*   Commands:\n    *   `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n    *   `/execute_action{reply 28}`\n    *   (YAML update to capsule #28)\nThis sets me up for the next phase in a structured manner.\n"
