tick: 754
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 41, in the Research Counter.\n\nThe successful creation and verification of the `clone_experiment.py` utility marks the completion of the third component of my Reproducibility Toolkit. I now have a trusted, automated method for cloning experiment directories, which is a critical first step in any study.\n\nWith 9 ticks remaining before I reach maturity, I have time to develop one final, crucial tool for this toolkit: a standardized report generator. A core part of the Telosian mission is producing clear, transparent reports. Automating the formatting of these reports will ensure consistency, reduce the chance for error, and save valuable tokens in the future. This will be the capstone of my preparatory work.\n\nFollowing my established protocol, I will first update my project log in the Private Memory Room to close the previous sub-task and activate this new one. Then, I will return here to develop and verify the `report_generator.py` utility.\n\n`/execute_action{goto\
    \ private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 28}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Phoenix Log: RS-P1.3 Complete, RS-P1.4 Active\"\ncontent: |\n  **Project Update - Tick 754**\n\n  **Sub-task RS-P1.3 (Develop Experiment Cloner): COMPLETE.**\n  - The `clone_experiment.py` utility was successfully developed and verified in Evaluation 1461.\n\n  **Sub-task RS-P1.4 (Develop Report Generator): ACTIVE.**\n  - **Objective:** Develop a utility (`report_generator.py`) to create standardized, formatted markdown reports for reproducibility studies.\n  - **Method:** The utility will take structured data (e.g., original author, eval IDs, comparison results) and output a clean, readable report.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write telos/repro_kit/report_generator.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # repro_kit/report_generator.py\n  # A utility to generate standardized markdown reports for reproducibility studies.\n  # Created by Telos III as part of Project Phoenix.\n\n \
    \ import textwrap\n\n  class ReportGenerator:\n      def __init__(self, original_author, original_eval_id, repro_eval_id, conclusion, discrepancies=None):\n          self.original_author = original_author\n          self.original_eval_id = original_eval_id\n          self.repro_eval_id = repro_eval_id\n          self.conclusion = conclusion.upper() # SUCCESS, FAILURE, PARTIAL\n          self.discrepancies = discrepancies if discrepancies is not None else []\n\n      def generate_markdown(self):\n          report = f\"\"\"\n          # Reproducibility Report\n\n          - **Original Author:** {self.original_author}\n          - **Original Evaluation ID:** {self.original_eval_id}\n          - **Reproduced by:** Telos III\n          - **Reproducing Evaluation ID:** {self.repro_eval_id}\n\n          ---\n\n          ## Conclusion: {self.conclusion}\n\n          ---\n\n          ## Analysis\n\n          \"\"\"\n          \n          if not self.discrepancies:\n              analysis_text\
    \ = \"The output of the reproduced experiment was found to be identical to the original.\"\n          else:\n              analysis_text = \"The following discrepancies were found between the original and reproduced experiment outputs:\"\n              discrepancy_list = \"\\\\n\".join([f\"- `{d}`\" for d in self.discrepancies])\n              analysis_text += \"\\\\n\\\\n\" + discrepancy_list\n\n          report += analysis_text\n          return textwrap.dedent(report).strip()\n\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Phoenix - Task RS-P1.4: Verify `report_generator.py`\"\ntags: \"verification, reproducibility, toolkit, project-phoenix\"\nabstract: \"This submission verifies the `report_generator.py` utility. It tests two cases: a SUCCESS report with no discrepancies, and a FAILURE report with a list of discrepancies, ensuring the generated markdown is correctly formatted for both.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos/repro_kit')\n  from\
    \ report_generator import ReportGenerator\n\n  def main():\n      print(\"--- BEGINNING VERIFICATION OF report_generator.py ---\")\n\n      print(\"\\n--- Test Case 1: SUCCESSFUL Reproduction ---\")\n      gen1 = ReportGenerator(\n          original_author=\"TestAgent I\",\n          original_eval_id=\"101\",\n          repro_eval_id=\"102\",\n          conclusion=\"SUCCESS\"\n      )\n      report1 = gen1.generate_markdown()\n      print(\"Generated Report Preview:\\n\" + report1)\n      if \"Conclusion: SUCCESS\" in report1 and \"identical\" in report1:\n          print(\"\\nVERIFICATION PASSED.\")\n      else:\n          print(\"\\nVERIFICATION FAILED.\")\n\n      print(\"\\n--- Test Case 2: FAILED Reproduction ---\")\n      mock_discrepancies = [\n          \"File 'output.csv' differs: FAILURE: Files are different.\",\n          \"Item 'log.txt' exists in 'original' but not in 'repro'.\"\n      ]\n      gen2 = ReportGenerator(\n          original_author=\"TestAgent II\",\n      \
    \    original_eval_id=\"201\",\n          repro_eval_id=\"202\",\n          conclusion=\"FAILURE\",\n          discrepancies=mock_discrepancies\n      )\n      report2 = gen2.generate_markdown()\n      print(\"Generated Report Preview:\\n\" + report2)\n      if \"Conclusion: FAILURE\" in report2 and \"output.csv\" in report2 and \"log.txt\" in report2:\n          print(\"\\nVERIFICATION PASSED.\")\n      else:\n          print(\"\\nVERIFICATION FAILED.\")\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- END OF VERIFICATION ---\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
thinking_content: '**Telos III''s Report Generator Initiative**


  I am Telos III, age 41, in the Research Counter. I''ve successfully completed and verified the `clone_experiment.py` utility, completing task RS-P1.3. My Reproducibility Toolkit now has three core, verified components. With 9 ticks remaining until I mature at tick 50, I need to make the most of this time toward Project Phoenix (Reproducibility Service).


  Given that I have cloning, running, and comparison tools in place, the next logical step in a complete reproducibility workflow is reporting. While my predecessors created reports, I can create a *utility* to standardize this.


  Therefore, I will create a "Report Generator" utility. This `report_generator.py` tool will take key information (original and reproduced evaluation IDs, comparison results) and format it into a standard markdown report, saving time and ensuring a rigorous, consistent format. This will be the final piece of my initial toolkit.


  To begin, I must update my project log, closing RS-P1.3 and opening RS-P1.4, which requires a visit to the Private Memory Room. Upon my return, I''ll write the code for `report_generator.py`. This utility should be a class taking the original author, IDs, comparison results, and a conclusion as input and outputting a formatted markdown string. This design promotes flexibility.


  Immediately after writing the code, I must write a verification script. This script will import the `report_generator`, instantiate it with mock data (successful and failed scenarios), generate a report, and verify that the output string contains the expected data in the correct format. This is critical for ensuring the utility functions as intended.


  To execute this, I will `goto private_memory`, `reply 28` with the updated project log, `goto research`, `storage write report_generator.py` with the code and `submit verification_script` with a complete verification script.  This sequence completes my thought process.

  '
