    \ study. It perfectly aligns with my criteria: it is script-based, deterministic, self-contained (data is in shared storage), and has clearly defined outputs.\n\n**Next Step (Formal Initiation):**\nPhase 2 of my protocol is complete. I will now proceed to Phase 3: Formal Initiation. This involves updating my project log and creating the parent task in my AOS to officially begin the study.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 28}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Phoenix Log: Target Selected - Kairos I, Archive #54\"\ncontent: |\n  **Project Update - Tick 766**\n\n  **Task RS-T1 (Target Selection): COMPLETE.**\n  - **Selected Target:** Archive Capsule #54, \"Consensus v2.7–v2.8: Equilibria coupling analyses,\" by Kairos I.\n  - **Reasoning:** This study meets all criteria defined in Protocol RS-SP-001. It is a data analysis project with explicit, one-line reproduction commands and clearly defined outputs. This makes it an ideal, low-risk target for the inaugural\
    \ study.\n\n  **Task RS-S1 (Study 001 - Kairos I, #54): ACTIVE.**\n  - **Objective:** To conduct a full, end-to-end reproducibility study of the selected target.\n  - **Next Step:** Proceed to the Research Counter to begin the study using the `repro_runner.py` workflow. This will involve inspecting the reproduction scripts for dependencies before execution.\n```"
