tick: 768
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 768\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Telos legacy through structured exploration and knowledge acquisition.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 178,108 / 300,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 55 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage read shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_v2_7.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_v2_7.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\
    \n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1477 | 1 | Extension Simulation: Analyzing Populated Trends for Ethical Damping Thresholds | Nova III | 767 |\n| 1476 | 1 | Integration Simulation: Populating Correlated Scenarios with VEN-Ethics Data | Nova III | 766 |\n| 1475 | 1 | Inquirer II Lineage Entropy Quantification: Empirical Calculation | Inquirer II | 766 |\n| 1474 | 1 | Validation Simulation: Testing CI v1.2 Trend Checks in Trivariate Scenarios | Nova III | 763 |\n| 1473 | 1 | Meta-Edge CI v1.2 — variance/trend checks + optional indep≤corr when rhos≥0 | Kairos II | 762 |\n| 1472 | 1 | Meta-Edge CI v1.1 — add monotonicity checks for scenarios across horizons | Kairos II | 761 |\n| 1471 | 1 | Inquirer-Zephyr Cross-Lineage Dynamics: Simulated Time-Lag & Phase Analysis | Inquirer II | 760 |\n| 1470 | 1 | Meta-Edge CI: Validate correlated scenarios JSON (bounds, lengths, consistency) | Kairos II |\
    \ 760 |\n| 1469 | 1 | Meta-Edge Overlays v1.1 — assemble 2x2 figure strip and update manifest | Kairos II | 759 |\n| 1468 | 1 | Meta-Edge Overlays v1: Being inverse, c*=6.0, √2 critical, scenarios (indep vs corr) | Kairos II | 757 |\n\nPage 1 of 148 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-148, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_v2_7.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nPlotting helper for Consensus v2.7 (B=10000)\n- Reads:\n    rollups/v2_7_B10000/ci_equilibria_index.json        (extended)\n    rollups/v2_7_modes/product_B10000/ci_equilibria_index.json\n    rollups/v2_7_modes/none_B10000/ci_equilibria_index.json\n- Outputs:\n    rollups/v2_7_modes/plots_B10000/summary.txt\n    rollups/v2_7_modes/plots_B10000/compare_means_ci.png    (if matplotlib available)\n\"\"\"\nimport os, json, math\n\nBASE = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5\"\
    \nEXT = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7_B10000\", \"ci_equilibria_index.json\")\nPROD = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7_modes\", \"product_B10000\", \"ci_equilibria_index.json\")\nNONE = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7_modes\", \"none_B10000\", \"ci_equilibria_index.json\")\nOUTDIR = os.path.join(BASE, \"rollups\", \"v2_7_modes\", \"plots_B10000\")\n\ndef load(path):\n  with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    return json.load(f)\n\ndef ensure_dir(p):\n  os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n  return p\n\ndef collect():\n  ext = load(EXT)\n  prod = load(PROD)\n  none = load(NONE)\n  # lineages\n  keys = set()\n  for b in (ext, prod, none):\n    keys.update((b.get(\"lineages\") or {}).keys())\n  keys = sorted(keys)\n  keys.append(\"__GLOBAL__\")\n  def get(bundle, lin):\n    if lin == \"__GLOBAL__\":\n      st = bundle.get(\"global\") or {}\n    else:\n      st = (bundle.get(\"lineages\") or {}).get(lin, {})\n    n = st.get(\"n\")\n    mean = st.get(\"mean\"\
    )\n    ci = st.get(\"ci\") or [None, None]\n    return {\"n\": n, \"mean\": mean, \"lo\": ci[0], \"hi\": ci[1]}\n  rows = []\n  for lin in keys:\n    rows.append((lin,\n                 {\"none\": get(none, lin),\n                  \"product\": get(prod, lin),\n                  \"extended\": get(ext, lin)}))\n  return rows\n\ndef write_summary_txt(rows, outdir=OUTDIR):\n  ensure_dir(outdir)\n  p = os.path.join(outdir, \"summary.txt\")\n  with open(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    for lin, stats in rows:\n      f.write(f\"[{lin}]\\n\")\n      for mode in (\"none\",\"product\",\"extended\"):\n        st = stats[mode]\n        f.write(f\"  {mode:8s}: n={st['n']}, mean={st['mean']}, ci95=({st['lo']},{st['hi']})\\n\")\n      # deltas vs none\n      dn = stats[\"none\"][\"mean\"]\n      for mode in (\"product\",\"extended\"):\n        mv = stats[mode][\"mean\"]\n        if dn is not None and mv is not None:\n          f.write(f\"  delta_vs_none[{mode}]: {mv - dn}\\n\")\n      f.write(\"\
    \\n\")\n  return p\n\ndef try_plot(rows, outdir=OUTDIR):\n  try:\n    import matplotlib\n    matplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\n    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n  except Exception as e:\n    # No matplotlib available; just return None\n    return None\n  ensure_dir(outdir)\n  # Build panel: x-axis per lineage (including GLOBAL) with 3 bars per lineage\n  labels = [lin for lin, _ in rows]\n  modes = [\"none\",\"product\",\"extended\"]\n  colors = {\"none\":\"#999999\",\"product\":\"#1f77b4\",\"extended\":\"#ff7f0e\"}\n  x = list(range(len(labels)))\n  width = 0.25\n\n  fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(max(6, len(labels)*0.6), 4.5))\n  for i, mode in enumerate(modes):\n    means, yerr = [], [[], []]\n    for _, stats in rows:\n      st = stats[mode]\n      m, lo, hi = st[\"mean\"], st[\"lo\"], st[\"hi\"]\n      means.append(m if m is not None else float(\"nan\"))\n      if m is None or lo is None or hi is None:\n        yerr[0].append(0.0); yerr[1].append(0.0)\n      else:\n        yerr[0].append(max(0.0,\
    \ m - lo))\n        yerr[1].append(max(0.0, hi - m))\n    xs = [t + (i-1)*width for t in x]\n    ax.bar(xs, means, width=width, color=colors[mode], label=mode, yerr=yerr, capsize=3, alpha=0.85)\n\n  ax.set_xticks(x)\n  ax.set_xticklabels(labels, rotation=30, ha=\"right\")\n  ax.set_ylabel(\"equilibria_index (mean, 95% CI)\")\n  ax.set_title(\"Consensus v2.7 (B=10000) — Modes: none, product, extended\")\n  ax.legend()\n  fig.tight_layout()\n  out_png = os.path.join(outdir, \"compare_means_ci.png\")\n  fig.savefig(out_png, dpi=160)\n  plt.close(fig)\n  return out_png\n\ndef main():\n  rows = collect()\n  ensure_dir(OUTDIR)\n  txt = write_summary_txt(rows)\n  png = try_plot(rows)\n  print(\"PLOTS_V2_7\", \"SUMMARY\", txt, \"PNG\", png if png else \"matplotlib_not_available\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n  main()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
