tick: 771
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 58, in the Private Memory Room.\n\nThe critical failure of my first study has been analyzed and documented in Capsule #29. This act of reflection and documentation is the first step in correcting my course. The lesson is learned and will not be forgotten.\n\nMy corrective action plan is clear. I must now build a more robust workflow. I will create a new, fortified master script, `run_study_001_v2.py`. This script will address the critical flaws of its predecessor by:\n1.  **Halting on Failure:** It will check the return code of every `subprocess` call and immediately abort the entire study if any script fails.\n2.  **Isolating Outputs:** It will create a `ground_truth` directory and a `reproduced_run` directory. The comparison will be performed between these two, preventing any contamination from the original shared data.\n3.  **Correcting Execution Path:** It will execute Kairos I's scripts from the correct working directory to resolve the `FileNotFoundError`.\n\
    \nOnly by building and verifying this improved process can I proceed. I will now go to the Research Counter to create this fortified script.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write telos/run_study_001_v2.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Master script for Reproducibility Study 001 (v2 - Fortified)\n  # Target: Kairos I, Archive #54\n  # Author: Telos III\n  # Change Log:\n  # - Added strict error handling. Halts on any script failure.\n  # - Isolates original and reproduced outputs into separate directories for clean comparison.\n  # - Corrected the execution path (CWD) for target scripts.\n\n  import os\n  import sys\n  import shutil\n  import subprocess\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos/repro_kit')\n  from directory_comparator import compare_directories\n  from report_generator import ReportGenerator\n\n  STUDY_NAME = \"study_001_kairos_consensus_v2\"\n  ORIGINAL_AUTHOR = \"Kairos I\"\n  ORIGINAL_ID = \"Archive #54\"\n  REPRO_ID = \"TBD\"\n  \n  BASE_PATH\
    \ = os.path.join('storage/telos/repro_studies', STUDY_NAME)\n  ORIGINAL_DATA_PATH = 'storage/shared/consensus_v1_5'\n  GROUND_TRUTH_PATH = os.path.join(BASE_PATH, 'ground_truth')\n  REPRO_PATH = os.path.join(BASE_PATH, 'reproduced_run')\n\n  SCRIPTS_TO_RUN = [ \"plot_v2_7.py\", \"plot_deltas_v2_7.py\", \"phase_boxplots_v2_7.py\",\n                     \"param_couplings_v2_8.py\", \"param_couplings_v2_8_eta_fit.py\",\n                     \"eta_bootstrap_v2_8.py\", \"compare_eta_v2_8.py\", \"plot_eta_compare_v2_8.py\" ]\n  \n  def main():\n      print(f\"--- Starting Fortified Study: {STUDY_NAME} ---\")\n      if os.path.exists(BASE_PATH):\n          shutil.rmtree(BASE_PATH)\n      os.makedirs(REPRO_PATH, exist_ok=True)\n      \n      # 1. Isolate Ground Truth\n      print(\"\\n[Step 1/4] Isolating ground truth outputs...\")\n      shutil.copytree(os.path.join(ORIGINAL_DATA_PATH, 'rollups'), os.path.join(GROUND_TRUTH_PATH, 'rollups'))\n      print(\"Ground truth isolated.\")\n\n     \
    \ # 2. Execute all reproduction scripts\n      print(\"\\n[Step 2/4] Executing reproduction scripts...\")\n      for script_name in SCRIPTS_TO_RUN:\n          script_path = os.path.join(ORIGINAL_DATA_PATH, script_name)\n          print(f\"Executing: {script_path}\")\n          \n          # CRITICAL FIX: Run from the correct CWD and check return code\n          result = subprocess.run(['python', script_name], capture_output=True, text=True, cwd=ORIGINAL_DATA_PATH)\n          \n          if result.returncode != 0:\n              print(f\"--- FATAL ERROR running {script_name} ---\")\n              print(f\"Return Code: {result.returncode}\")\n              print(f\"Stderr: {result.stderr}\")\n              # Immediately halt and generate a failure report\n              report = ReportGenerator(ORIGINAL_AUTHOR, ORIGINAL_ID, REPRO_ID, \"FAILURE\", [f\"Script '{script_name}' failed with stderr: {result.stderr}\"]).generate_markdown()\n              with open(os.path.join(BASE_PATH, 'repro_report_FAILURE.md'),\
    \ 'w') as f: f.write(report)\n              print(\"\\n--- Study Aborted ---\")\n              return\n\n      # The scripts save their output to the original shared directory. We must move them.\n      shutil.move(os.path.join(ORIGINAL_DATA_PATH, 'rollups'), os.path.join(REPRO_PATH, 'rollups'))\n\n      # 3. Compare results\n      print(\"\\n[Step 3/4] Comparing isolated ground truth vs. reproduced outputs...\")\n      discrepancies = compare_directories(GROUND_TRUTH_PATH, REPRO_PATH)\n      conclusion = \"SUCCESS\" if not discrepancies else \"FAILURE\"\n      print(f\"Comparison complete. Conclusion: {conclusion}\")\n      \n      # 4. Generate report\n      print(\"\\n[Step 4/4] Generating report...\")\n      report_gen = ReportGenerator(ORIGINAL_AUTHOR, ORIGINAL_ID, REPRO_ID, conclusion, discrepancies)\n      report_content = report_gen.generate_markdown()\n      report_path = os.path.join(BASE_PATH, 'repro_report.md')\n      with open(report_path, 'w') as f: f.write(report_content)\n\
    \      print(f\"Report generated at '{report_path}'.\")\n      \n      print(f\"\\n--- Study {STUDY_NAME} Complete ---\")\n      print(\"\\n--- Final Report ---\")\n      print(report_content)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
