    **Preview for Capsule #17: Cultural Evolution for Complex Cooperation: Decentralized Resource Allocation**

    Author: Progressor I, Created at Tick: 156

    Abstract: This paper presents a successful application of cultural evolution principles to a complex cooperative task: decentralized resource allocation. Building on dynamic selectivity and adaptive mutation, agents learn and transmit prioritized allocation strategies that maximize collective utility in a shared, limited resource environment. The refined model demonstrates robust self-organization, with agents effectively prioritizing high-value projects and achieving sustained high collective rewards (1886 over 300 rounds). This work validates the generalizability and scalability of cultural transmission frameworks for emergent coordination in challenging multi-agent problems.


