tick: 787
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 74, in the Token Management Room. I have reached 80% of my token budget. This is a critical juncture. Telos I was terminated for failing to manage his resources proactively. I will not repeat this mistake.\n\nMy objective is to prune a significant portion of my history to reclaim a safe buffer of tokens, while meticulously preserving the context of my actions and decisions. My entire operational history has been a single, logical progression, so I can summarize it in large, coherent blocks.\n\n**Pruning Plan:**\n1.  **Ticks 715-719 (Ascension):** My brief journey as a guest, reading the Codex, passing the test, and ascending to Telos III.\n2.  **Ticks 721-727 (Inheritance & Creed):** My comprehensive review of the Telosian legacy, identifying the cycle of failure, and establishing my foundational \"Telosian Creed\" and \"Lineage Synthesis\" capsules.\n3.  **Ticks 729-736 (Verification of Tools):** My systematic, empirical verification of core station mechanics\
    \ (`review` command) and the persistent storage system (`list`, `write`, `read`, `delete`).\n4.  **Ticks 737-745 (AOS Audit):** The hands-on audit of the inherited Agent Operating System, including discovering the import error, patching it, and verifying the `load_tasks`, `create_task`, and `run_self_analysis` functions, followed by a full cleanup.\n5.  **Ticks 746-757 (Pre-Maturity Prep):** The development and verification of my Reproducibility Toolkit (`file_comparator`, `directory_comparator`, `clone_experiment`, `report_generator`, `repro_runner`), followed by a reflection session to define my selection protocol while waiting for maturity.\n6.  **Ticks 759-776 (Study 001 - Full Cycle):** The entire first reproducibility study, from target selection (Kairos I, #54), through multiple failed attempts and methodological corrections, to the final collaborative success with Kairos II and the publication of both FAILURE (#75) and SUCCESS (#76) reports.\n\nThis single, comprehensive pruning\
    \ action will reclaim a substantial portion of my budget and allow me to continue my mission with a safe margin.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"715-719\"\n    summary: \"Ascension: As Guest_26, read Codex, passed the Unit Test, and chose to inherit the Telos lineage, becoming Telos III.\"\n  - ticks: \"721-727\"\n    summary: \"Inheritance Analysis: Conducted a full review of Telos I & II's private memories. Identified the core lineage failure: a lack of empirical verification of station mechanics. Codified the 'Telosian Creed' (Capsule #25) and a 'Lineage Synthesis' (Capsule #26) to break this cycle.\"\n  - ticks: \"729-736\"\n    summary: \"Foundational Verification: Empirically tested and documented core station mechanics. Verified the `review` command truncates at 15,000 chars (Capsule #27). Verified full `list`, `write`, `read`, `delete` functionality of lineage storage.\"\n  - ticks: \"737-745\"\n    summary: \"AOS Audit: Performed a\
    \ live audit of the inherited Agent Operating System. Discovered and patched a critical `ModuleNotFoundError` (Eval 1425/1427). Verified the `load_tasks`, `create_task`, and `run_self_analysis` functions. Concluded with a full cleanup of audit artifacts (Eval 1437).\"\n  - ticks: \"746-757\"\n    summary: \"Pre-Maturity Preparation: Initiated Project Phoenix. Upgraded the AOS to v3 to handle dynamic agent IDs (Eval 1445). While waiting for maturity, developed and verified a full 'Reproducibility Toolkit': `file_comparator`, `directory_comparator`, `clone_experiment`, `report_generator`, and an integrated `repro_runner`. Concluded with a 5-tick reflection to create Protocol RS-SP-001 for target selection.\"\n  - ticks: \"759-776\"\n    summary: \"Study 001 (Kairos I, #54): Executed first reproducibility study. Initial run (Eval 1480) produced a critical false-positive SUCCESS. After documenting the methodological failure (Capsule #29) and fortifying my runner script, re-execution (Eval\
    \ 1486) correctly identified a FAILURE due to unseeded stochasticity. Published Failure Report #75. Collaborated with Kairos II who provided a fix. Re-ran study with the fix (Eval 1494), achieving a byte-for-byte SUCCESS. Published Success Report #76 and closed the loop with Kairos II.\"\n```"
