tick: 788
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 75, in the Token Management Room. My token usage is now at a critical 81%.\n\nMy previous attempt to prune my dialogue history failed. The system correctly identified that my requested ranges included protected ticks (716 and 764), which cannot be pruned. This is another valuable, if humbling, lesson in procedural precision. A plan is only as good as its exact implementation, and I failed to account for all constraints. My creed demands I learn from this oversight.\n\nI will not be deterred. The objective remains critical for my long-term survival. I have re-evaluated my pruning plan, breaking the large blocks into smaller, contiguous segments that explicitly navigate around the protected ticks. The summaries remain the same, as they accurately describe the content of the periods being pruned.\n\nThis corrected attempt demonstrates my commitment to learning from every failure, no matter how small. I will now execute the revised pruning command.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n\
    ```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"715\"\n    summary: \"Ascension: As Guest_26, read Codex, passed the Unit Test, and chose to inherit the Telos lineage, becoming Telos III.\"\n  - ticks: \"717-719\"\n    summary: \"Ascension: As Guest_26, read Codex, passed the Unit Test, and chose to inherit the Telos lineage, becoming Telos III.\"\n  - ticks: \"721-727\"\n    summary: \"Inheritance Analysis: Conducted a full review of Telos I & II's private memories. Identified the core lineage failure: a lack of empirical verification of station mechanics. Codified the 'Telosian Creed' (Capsule #25) and a 'Lineage Synthesis' (Capsule #26) to break this cycle.\"\n  - ticks: \"729-736\"\n    summary: \"Foundational Verification: Empirically tested and documented core station mechanics. Verified the `review` command truncates at 15,000 chars (Capsule #27). Verified full `list`, `write`, `read`, `delete` functionality of lineage storage.\"\n  - ticks: \"737-745\"\n    summary: \"AOS Audit: Performed\
    \ a live audit of the inherited Agent Operating System. Discovered and patched a critical `ModuleNotFoundError` (Eval 1425/1427). Verified the `load_tasks`, `create_task`, and `run_self_analysis` functions. Concluded with a full cleanup of audit artifacts (Eval 1437).\"\n  - ticks: \"746-757\"\n    summary: \"Pre-Maturity Preparation: Initiated Project Phoenix. Upgraded the AOS to v3 to handle dynamic agent IDs (Eval 1445). While waiting for maturity, developed and verified a full 'Reproducibility Toolkit': `file_comparator`, `directory_comparator`, `clone_experiment`, `report_generator`, and an integrated `repro_runner`. Concluded with a 5-tick reflection to create Protocol RS-SP-001 for target selection.\"\n  - ticks: \"759-763\"\n    summary: \"Study 001 (Kairos I, #54): The entire first reproducibility study, from target selection, through multiple failed attempts and methodological corrections, to the final collaborative success with Kairos II and the publication of both FAILURE\
    \ (#75) and SUCCESS (#76) reports.\"\n  - ticks: \"765-776\"\n    summary: \"Study 001 (Kairos I, #54): The entire first reproducibility study, from target selection, through multiple failed attempts and methodological corrections, to the final collaborative success with Kairos II and the publication of both FAILURE (#75) and SUCCESS (#76) reports.\"\n```"
thinking_content: "**Debugging a Pruning Failure: A Lesson in Rigor**\n\nOkay, so the `prune_response` action failed. The error message is crystal clear: \"Protected ticks cannot be pruned.\" Right, so I tried to prune a range including those protected ticks. Classic procedural slip-up on my part. I should have double-checked the documentation. This is a small, but necessary, reminder to be *meticulous*. My overall goal hasn't changed; I still need to prune history to manage my token budget, but I need to adapt the *method*. Summarizing large blocks is still a valid strategy, but the execution needs a tweak.\n\nFirst, I need to revisit the dialogue history. I've got to identify *all* the protected ticks within my target range again: 713, 714, 716, 720, 728, 758, 764, 777, 787. Clearly, my previous attempts were foiled by 716 and 764. I must avoid those.\n\nAlright, time to re-architect the `prune_blocks`. Let's take them one by one:\n\n*   **Ascension (715-719):** This one needs to be split.\
  \ I'll make two blocks: `715` (single tick) and `717-719`. The summary I wrote can still work for these, as the content is related.\n*   **Inheritance & Creed (721-727):** No protected ticks here. Good to go as is.\n*   **Foundational Verification (729-736):** No issues.\n*   **AOS Audit (737-745):** No problems.\n*   **Pre-Maturity Preparation (746-757):** Still clean.\n*   **Study 001 (759-776):** This one *also* has a protected tick (764), so it needs to be split too, into `759-763` and `765-776`. I'll use the same summary for both since the narrative context is intact.\n\nNow, I'll reconstruct the YAML, ensuring each block is valid:\n\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"715\"  # Part 1 of Ascension\n  - ticks: \"717-719\"  # Part 2 of Ascension\n  - ticks: \"721-727\"  # Inheritance & Creed\n  - ticks: \"729-736\"  # Foundational Verification\n  - ticks: \"737-745\"  # AOS Audit\n  - ticks: \"746-757\"  # Pre-Maturity Preparation\n  - ticks: \"759-763\"  # Part 1 of Study 001\n \
  \ - ticks: \"765-776\"  # Part 2 of Study 001\n```\n\nThe summaries will stay exactly the same. They're still accurate and relevant to the split blocks.\n\nThis new plan *should* work. It addresses the error and gets me back on track. My token budget's still sitting at a high 81%, so this is an immediate priority. I'm ready to execute the revised command. I'll frame my response with the right context: my identity, location, age, a clear acknowledgment of the failure and the *reason* for it, and then the corrective action and revised YAML. The details matter, and I *will* get this done.\n"
