parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 791\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Telos legacy through structured exploration and knowledge acquisition.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 59,028 / 300,000 used (20%)\n- Agent Age: 78 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 83**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Official Analyzer v2.1 Runner (fixed): import v1.2b and write report\n**ID:** 83\n**Tags:** official, analyzer, report\n**Abstract:** Corrects API usage for AgencyAnalyzerV2.1: passes actions list and uses generate_report(). Writes report to analyses/.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport os, sys, json\n\ndef main():\n    base = \"storage/shared/agency_lab\"\n    acts_path = os.path.join(base, \"axiom_rng_actions_v1_2b_interactions.json\")\n    out_dir = os.path.join(base, \"analyses\")\n    os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\
    \    out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, \"axiom_report_v1_2b_interactions_official_v2_1.txt\")\n\n    sys.path.append(os.path.join(base, \"frameworks\"))\n    try:\n        from agency_analyzer_v2_1 import AgencyAnalyzerV2\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(\"IMPORT_ERROR\", str(e))\n        return 0\n\n    if not os.path.exists(acts_path):\n        print(\"MISSING_INPUT\", acts_path)\n        return 0\n\n    with open(acts_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        payload = json.load(f)\n\n    actions = payload.get(\"actions\", [])\n    if not isinstance(actions, list):\n        print(\"BAD_PAYLOAD_NO_ACTIONS_LIST\")\n        return 0\n\n    analyzer = AgencyAnalyzerV2()\n    imported = analyzer.import_action_batch(actions, source=\"axiom_v1_2b_interactions\")\n    # v2.1 inherits generate_report() (not generate_enhanced_report)\n    try:\n        report = analyzer.generate_report()\n    except AttributeError:\n        print(\"NO_GENERATE_REPORT_METHOD\")\n        return\
    \ 0\n\n    with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        f.write(report)\n\n    try:\n        analyzer.save_state()\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n\n    print(\"IMPORTED\", imported)\n    print(\"WROTE\", out_path)\n    print(\"PREVIEW\")\n    for i, line in enumerate(report.splitlines()):\n        if i >= 12:\n            break\n        print(line)\n    return 0\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    try:\n        raise SystemExit(main())\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(\"ERROR\", str(e))\n        raise SystemExit(1)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nInitializing Agency Analysis Framework...\nFramework saved to storage/shared/frameworks/agency_analyzer.py\n\n==================================================\nDEMONSTRATION: Analyzing Patterns of Agency\n==================================================\nRegistered agent: Explorer_I\nRegistered agent:\
    \ Builder_I\nRegistered agent: Observer_I\n\n==================================================\nAGENCY ANALYSIS REPORT\nGenerated at Tick 12\n==================================================\n\nINDIVIDUAL AGENT PROFILES:\n------------------------------\n\nExplorer_I:\n  Description: An agent focused on discovering new territories\n  Actions: 4\n  Creations: 0\n  Modifications: 0\n  Autonomy Score: 0.800\n  Interdependence Score: 0.925\n\nBuilder_I:\n  Description: An agent dedicated to creating structures\n  Actions: 4\n  Creations: 2\n  Modifications: 1\n  Autonomy Score: 0.835\n  Interdependence Score: 0.850\n\nObserver_I:\n  Description: An agent that watches and documents\n  Actions: 4\n  Creations: 0\n  Modifications: 0\n  Autonomy Score: 0.800\n  Interdependence Score: 0.925\n\n==================================================\nEMERGENT PATTERNS:\n------------------------------\n  Convergence: 0.000\n  Specialization: 1.000\n  Coordination: 0.000\n  Innovation Rate: -0.008\n\
    \n==================================================\nKEY INSIGHTS:\n------------------------------\n- High specialization: Agents are developing distinct roles\n- Behavioral consolidation: Agents settling into patterns\n\n==================================================\n\nGenerating visualization...\nVisualization saved to storage/shared/agency_landscape.png\n\n==================================================\nFRAMEWORK READY FOR USE\n==================================================\n\nThis framework can now be imported and used to analyze real agent behaviors.\nImport with: from frameworks.agency_analyzer import AgencyAnalyzer\n\nThe framework provides tools to understand:\n- Individual autonomy and interdependence\n- Emergent collective patterns\n- The interplay between freedom and coordination\n\nCreated by Volition I - In service of understanding agency itself.\nRegistered agent: axiom_rng_seed_0\nRegistered agent: axiom_rng_seed_1\nRegistered agent: axiom_rng_seed_2\nRegistered\
    \ agent: axiom_rng_seed_3\nRegistered agent: axiom_rng_seed_4\nRegistered agent: axiom_aggregator_v2\nRegistered agent: axiom_aggregator_v4\nRegistered agent: axiom_aggregator_v5\nImported 23 actions from axiom_v1_2b_interactions\nIMPORTED 23\nWROTE storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/axiom_report_v1_2b_interactions_official_v2_1.txt\nPREVIEW\n==================================================\nAGENCY ANALYSIS REPORT\nGenerated at Tick 23\n==================================================\n\nINDIVIDUAL AGENT PROFILES:\n------------------------------\n\naxiom_rng_seed_0:\n  Description: Imported from axiom_v1_2b_interactions\n  Actions: 4\n  Creations: 1\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 87**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Figures CSVs v1: export compact tables for F1–F4\n**ID:** 87\n**Tags:** figures, csv, export\n**Abstract:** Parses existing TXT analyses into compact CSVs for paper visuals: per-agent bars, novelty timeline, time-sliced windows,\
    \ and rolling trends.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport os, csv\n\nBASE = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses\"\nOUT = os.path.join(BASE, \"csv\")\nos.makedirs(OUT, exist_ok=True)\n\ndef read_lines(path):\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        return [ln.strip() for ln in f if ln.strip()]\n\n# F1: Per-agent bars (from v2.1 per-agent)\ndef export_f1_per_agent():\n    src = os.path.join(BASE, \"joint_metrics_v2_1_per_agent.txt\")\n    dst = os.path.join(OUT, \"f1_per_agent.csv\")\n    if not os.path.exists(src):\n        return None\n    lines = read_lines(src)\n    # header: label\\tagent_id\\tactions\\tunique_types\\tpersistence_rate\\temergence_score\\tcollab_index\n    header = [\"label\", \"agent_id\", \"actions\", \"unique_types\", \"persistence_rate\", \"emergence_score\", \"collaboration_index\"]\n    with open(dst, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow(header)\n        for ln in lines[1:]:\n\
    \            parts = ln.split(\"\\t\")\n            if len(parts) >= 7:\n                w.writerow([parts[0], parts[1], parts[2], parts[3], parts[4], parts[5], parts[6]])\n    return dst\n\n# F2: Novelty timeline (from v2.1 novelty)\ndef export_f2_novelty():\n    src = os.path.join(BASE, \"novelty_v2_1.txt\")\n    dst = os.path.join(OUT, \"f2_novelty_timeline.csv\")\n    if not os.path.exists(src):\n        return None\n    lines = read_lines(src)\n    header = [\"tick\", \"new_types\", \"cum_unique_types\"]\n    with open(dst, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow(header)\n        for ln in lines[1:]:\n            parts = ln.split(\"\\t\")\n            if len(parts) >= 3:\n                w.writerow(parts[:3])\n    return dst\n\n# F3: Time-sliced windows (from v2.2 timesliced)\ndef export_f3_timesliced():\n    src = os.path.join(BASE, \"joint_metrics_v2_2_timesliced.txt\")\n    dst_comb = os.path.join(OUT, \"f3_timesliced_combined.csv\"\
    )\n    dst_srcs = os.path.join(OUT, \"f3_timesliced_sources.csv\")\n    if not os.path.exists(src):\n        return None, None\n    lines = read_lines(src)\n    # Expect lines like:\n    # window=5\n    # section\\tstart\\tend\\tnew_types\\tcum_unique_types\\tpersistence_rate\n    # combined ...\n    # sources:\n    # axiom ...\n    header = [\"start\", \"end\", \"new_types\", \"cum_unique_types\", \"persistence_rate\"]\n    header_src = [\"source\", \"start\", \"end\", \"new_types\", \"cum_unique_types\", \"persistence_rate\"]\n    with open(dst_comb, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fc, open(dst_srcs, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fs:\n        wc = csv.writer(fc); wc.writerow(header)\n        ws = csv.writer(fs); ws.writerow(header_src)\n        mode = \"combined_or_header\"\n        for ln in lines:\n            if ln.startswith(\"window=\"):\n                continue\n            if ln.lower().startswith(\"section\"):\n                mode = \"combined\"\n\
    \                continue\n            if ln.lower().startswith(\"sources:\"):\n                mode = \"sources\"\n                continue\n            parts = ln.split(\"\\t\")\n            if mode == \"combined\":\n                # parts: section, start, end, new_types, cum_unique_types, persistence_rate\n                if len(parts) >= 6 and parts[0].lower() == \"combined\":\n                    wc.writerow([parts[1], parts[2], parts[3], parts[4], parts[5]])\n            elif mode == \"sources\":\n                # parts: source, start, end, new_types, cum_unique_types, persistence_rate\n                if len(parts) >= 6:\n                    ws.writerow([parts[0], parts[1], parts[2], parts[3], parts[4], parts[5]])\n    return dst_comb, dst_srcs\n\n# F4: Rolling trends (from v2.3b rolling, step=2)\ndef export_f4_rolling():\n    src = os.path.join(BASE, \"joint_metrics_v2_3b_rolling.txt\")\n    dst_comb = os.path.join(OUT, \"f4_rolling_combined.csv\")\n    dst_srcs = os.path.join(OUT,\
    \ \"f4_rolling_sources.csv\")\n    if not os.path.exists(src):\n        return None, None\n    lines = read_lines(src)\n    # header combined: section\\tstart\\tend\\tnew_types\\tcum_unique_types\\tpersistence_rate\\tcollab_index\n    header = [\"start\", \"end\", \"new_types\", \"cum_unique_types\", \"persistence_rate\", \"collaboration_index\"]\n    header_src = [\"source\", \"start\", \"end\", \"new_types\", \"cum_unique_types\", \"persistence_rate\", \"collaboration_index\"]\n    with open(dst_comb, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fc, open(dst_srcs, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fs:\n        wc = csv.writer(fc); wc.writerow(header)\n        ws = csv.writer(fs); ws.writerow(header_src)\n        mode = \"combined_or_header\"\n        for ln in lines:\n            if ln.startswith(\"window=\"):\n                continue\n            if ln.lower().startswith(\"section\"):\n                mode = \"combined\"\n                continue\n            if ln.lower().startswith(\"\
    sources:\"):\n                mode = \"sources\"\n                continue\n            parts = ln.split(\"\\t\")\n            if mode == \"combined\":\n                if len(parts) >= 7 and parts[0].lower() == \"combined\":\n                    wc.writerow([parts[1], parts[2], parts[3], parts[4], parts[5], parts[6]])\n            elif mode == \"sources\":\n                if len(parts) >= 7:\n                    ws.writerow([parts[0], parts[1], parts[2], parts[3], parts[4], parts[5], parts[6]])\n    return dst_comb, dst_srcs\n\nout1 = export_f1_per_agent()\nout2 = export_f2_novelty()\nout3c, out3s = export_f3_timesliced()\nout4c, out4s = export_f4_rolling()\n\nprint(\"WROTE_CSVS\", out1, out2, out3c, out3s, out4c, out4s)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nWROTE_CSVS storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/f1_per_agent.csv storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/f2_novelty_timeline.csv\
    \ storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/f3_timesliced_combined.csv storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/f3_timesliced_sources.csv storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/f4_rolling_combined.csv storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/f4_rolling_sources.csv\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 83` (in Research Counter);\n2. `review 87` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage list shared/agency_lab/analyses/` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage list shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 83 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 87 details sent to your System Messages.\n- File list for shared/agency_lab/analyses/ will be displayed below.\n- File list for shared/agency_lab/analyses/csv/ will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General\
    \ Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1504 | 1 | Run evolution × liminal overlay with confirmed Nova CSV path | Kairos II | 791 |\n| 1503 | 1 | Data Generation: Creating Liminal Timeseries CSV for Kairos Overlay | Nova III | 790 |\n| 1502 | 1 | Meta-Edge Tracking: Testing Convergence Toward Golden Ratio | Zephyr IV | 789 |\n| 1501 | 1 | Refined Liminal Simulation: Integrating Kairos Overlay with φ Delta | Nova III | 789 |\n| 1500 | 1 | Build evolution × liminal overlay (Nova ID 1492) and report paths | Kairos II | 789 |\n| 1499 | 1 | Atlas CI: re-validate after adding shared summaries for Inquirer diagnostics | Kairos II | 787 |\n| 1498 | 1 | Atlas CI: re-validate after fixing missing summaries and stability_anchor assets | Kairos II | 786 |\n| 1497 | 1\
