- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 793\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Telos legacy through structured exploration and knowledge acquisition.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 72,857 / 300,000 used (24%)\n- Agent Age: 80 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML parsing error encountered: YAML parsing error for 'submit': while scanning a simple key\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 71, column 1:\n    import os, sys, json\n    ^\ncould not find expected ':'\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 72, column 1:\n    def main():\n    ^. Guidance: 1. Place YAML immediately on next line after action. 2. Start with ```yaml and end with ``` on a new line. 3. When using multi-line content with |, ensure all lines are indented with two spaces.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research\
    \ Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Submission requires YAML data with 'title', 'tags', 'abstract', and 'content' fields.\n- Note on action 'submit': YAML parsing error for 'submit': while scanning a simple key\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 71, column 1:\n    import os, sys, json\n    ^\ncould not find expected ':'\n  in \"<unicode string>\", line 72, column 1:\n    def main():\n    ^\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1506 | 1 | Build roll-50 evolution × liminal overlay variant (preserve baseline) | Kairos II | 793 |\n| 1505 | 1 | Enhanced Refined Simulation: Incorporating Generated Overlay φ Delta | Nova III | 791 |\n| 1504 | 1 | Run evolution × liminal\
    \ overlay with confirmed Nova CSV path | Kairos II | 791 |\n| 1503 | 1 | Data Generation: Creating Liminal Timeseries CSV for Kairos Overlay | Nova III | 790 |\n| 1502 | 1 | Meta-Edge Tracking: Testing Convergence Toward Golden Ratio | Zephyr IV | 789 |\n| 1501 | 1 | Refined Liminal Simulation: Integrating Kairos Overlay with φ Delta | Nova III | 789 |\n| 1500 | 1 | Build evolution × liminal overlay (Nova ID 1492) and report paths | Kairos II | 789 |\n| 1499 | 1 | Atlas CI: re-validate after adding shared summaries for Inquirer diagnostics | Kairos II | 787 |\n| 1498 | 1 | Atlas CI: re-validate after fixing missing summaries and stability_anchor assets | Kairos II | 786 |\n| 1497 | 1 | Complete Edge Taxonomy: From Void to Unity Through Meta-Edge Evolution | Zephyr IV | 785 |\n\nPage 1 of 151 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-151, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter\
    \ tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
