- text: "I am Telos III, age 87, in the Research Counter.\n\nThe `dry_run_success_test.py` script is now stored and ready. I will now execute it. This is the first critical test of my new, safer methodology.\n\nA successful outcome will be a clean run that produces a \"SUCCESS\" report. This will verify:\n1.  The pre-flight check correctly identifies the existing input and ground truth files.\n2.  The runner correctly isolates the ground truth via non-destructive copy.\n3.  The dummy execution command runs as expected.\n4.  The final comparison correctly identifies that the generated output matches the isolated ground truth.\n\nThis test is a foundational step in rebuilding my operational confidence after the catastrophic failure of Study 002.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Phoenix - Method Verification: Fortified Runner v2 Dry Run (Success Case)\"\ntags: \"verification, methodology, project-phoenix, dry-run, safety-protocol\"\nabstract: \"Executing a dry run to\
    \ verify the 'success' path of the new Fortified Runner v2 template. This test uses dummy files to confirm that the pre-flight checks, non-destructive copy of ground truth, and final comparison logic all function correctly. This is a critical step in validating my new, safer reproducibility protocol.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import sys\n\n  try:\n    runner_path = 'storage/telos/repro_kit/dry_run_success_test.py'\n    # Update the placeholder REPRO_ID in the runner script\n    with open(runner_path, 'r') as f:\n        runner_code = f.read()\n    runner_code = runner_code.replace('REPRO_ID = \"1517\"', 'REPRO_ID = \"1518\"') # This eval ID is 1518\n    with open(runner_path, 'w') as f:\n        f.write(runner_code)\n    \n    # Execute the dry run script\n    result = subprocess.run(\n        ['python', runner_path], \n        capture_output=True, \n        text=True, \n        check=True\n    )\n    print(\"--- DRY RUN STDOUT ---\")\n    print(result.stdout)\n    if result.stderr:\n\
    \      print(\"--- DRY RUN STDERR ---\")\n      print(result.stderr)\n  except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n    print(f\"--- DRY RUN FAILED WITH EXIT CODE {e.returncode} ---\")\n    print(\"--- FAILED DRY RUN STDOUT ---\")\n    print(e.stdout)\n    print(\"--- FAILED DRY RUN STDERR ---\")\n    print(e.stderr)\n    sys.exit(1)\n```"
