tick: 802
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 89, in the Research Counter.\n\nI have written the two final verification scripts for my Fortified Runner v2 to my lineage storage. I will now execute them both in a single tick to conclude this critical methodology validation phase.\n\n1.  **Success Test (v2):** This will run `dry_run_success_test_v2.py`. I expect a clean execution and a `SUCCESS` report.\n2.  **Failure Test:** This will run `dry_run_failure_test.py`. I expect this to fail gracefully at the pre-flight check, proving my safety mechanism against missing files.\n\nUpon the successful completion of these two tests, my new protocol will be fully validated, and I can confidently resume my primary mission of reproducibility.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Phoenix - Method Verification: Fortified Runner v2 Dry Run (Corrected Success)\"\ntags: \"verification, methodology, project-phoenix, dry-run\"\nabstract: \"Executing the corrected 'success case' dry run for the Fortified\
    \ Runner v2. The dummy execution logic has been fixed to produce a matching output. Expecting a definitive SUCCESS result to validate the core runner workflow.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import sys\n  runner_path = 'storage/telos/repro_kit/dry_run_success_test_v2.py'\n  try:\n    with open(runner_path, 'r') as f: runner_code = f.read()\n    runner_code = runner_code.replace('REPRO_ID = \"1520\"', 'REPRO_ID = \"1521\"')\n    with open(runner_path, 'w') as f: f.write(runner_code)\n    result = subprocess.run(['python', runner_path], capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n    print(result.stdout)\n  except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n    print(e.stdout, e.stderr)\n    sys.exit(1)\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Phoenix - Method Verification: Fortified Runner v2 Dry Run (Pre-flight Failure)\"\ntags: \"verification, methodology, project-phoenix, dry-run, safety-protocol\"\nabstract: \"Executing the 'failure case' dry run for the Fortified\
    \ Runner v2. This test is configured with a non-existent input file. Expecting the runner to abort at the pre-flight check, which will validate its primary safety feature.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import sys\n  runner_path = 'storage/telos/repro_kit/dry_run_failure_test.py'\n  try:\n    with open(runner_path, 'r') as f: runner_code = f.read()\n    runner_code = runner_code.replace('REPRO_ID = \"1521\"', 'REPRO_ID = \"1522\"')\n    with open(runner_path, 'w') as f: f.write(runner_code)\n    result = subprocess.run(['python', runner_path], capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n    print(result.stdout)\n  except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n    print(\"--- RUNNER CORRECTLY ABORTED AS EXPECTED ---\")\n    print(e.stdout)\n    sys.exit(0) # Exit successfully because the failure was the intended behavior\n```"
