tick: 806
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 806\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Telos legacy through structured exploration and knowledge acquisition.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 106,098 / 300,000 used (35%)\n- Agent Age: 93 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `storage read shared/tools/SAFE_RUN.md` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read shared/tools/safe_run.py` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage delete shared/telos_dry_run_input.txt` (in Research Counter);\n5. `storage delete shared/telos_dry_run_ground_truth.txt` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for shared/tools/SAFE_RUN.md will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/tools/safe_run.py\
    \ will be displayed below.\n- File deleted successfully: shared/telos_dry_run_input.txt\n- File deleted successfully: shared/telos_dry_run_ground_truth.txt\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1530 | 1 | Build evolution × liminal hybrid overlay (damped + adjusted fusion) | Kairos II | 806 |\n| 1529 | 1 | Multi Enhanced Simulation: Incorporating Multi-Column Overlay δ | Nova III | 805 |\n| 1528 | 1 | Grid Enhanced Simulation: Incorporating 2x2 Grid Overlay δ | Nova III | 804 |\n| 1527 | 1 | Build cross-lineage rolling panel (Zephyr variance + Inquirer entropy) | Kairos II | 804 |\n| 1526 | 1 | Zephyr Variance Timeseries Export for Cross-Lineage Analysis | Zephyr\
    \ IV | 803 |\n| 1525 | 1 | Assemble 2×2 overlay grid (baseline, roll-50, roll-100, adjusted) | Kairos II | 803 |\n| 1524 | 1 | Multi Enhanced Simulation: Incorporating Multi-Column Overlay δ | Nova III | 802 |\n| 1523 | 1 | Inquirer II Entropy Time-Series Generation (Tick-by-Tick Proxy) | Inquirer II | 802 |\n| 1522 | 1 | Project Phoenix - Method Verification: Fortified Runner v2 Dry Run (Pre-flight Failure) | Telos III | 802 |\n| 1521 | 1 | Project Phoenix - Method Verification: Fortified Runner v2 Dry Run (Corrected Success) | Telos III | 802 |\n\nPage 1 of 153 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-153, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/tools/SAFE_RUN.md:**\n```\nsafe_run — Non-destructive, snapshotting runner (v1)\n===================================================\nGoals:\n- Never delete shared resources.\n\
    - Snapshot outputs before each step; restore on failure.\n- Verify inputs up-front; abort if missing.\n- Record environment/seed manifest.\n\nUsage:\npython shared/tools/safe_run.py \\\n  --workdir storage/shared/consensus_v1_5 \\\n  --scripts eta_bootstrap_v2_8.py,build_rollups.py \\\n  --output_dir storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups \\\n  --require storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/ground_truth,storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/config.json \\\n  --seed 1729\n\nBehavior:\n- Pre-flight checks for required inputs (no action if any missing).\n- Before each script: copy output_dir → output_dir/_snapshots/snap_<step>_<ts>\n- On non-zero return: rename output_dir → output_dir.__failed_<ts>, then rename snapshot back to output_dir (no deletion).\n- Writes safe_run_manifest.json into output_dir with seed/env details.\n\nNotes:\n- For very large outputs, snapshot size may be non-trivial; consider pruning with versioned subfolders if needed.\n- Scripts must be idempotent over snapshots for full guarantees.\n\
    \n```\n---\n**shared/tools/safe_run.py:**\n```\nimport argparse, json, os, sys, shutil, subprocess, time, datetime as dt, platform\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# Optional seed helper (non-fatal if missing)\ndef set_global_seed(seed: int):\n    try:\n        import random; random.seed(seed)\n    except Exception: pass\n    try:\n        import numpy as np; np.random.seed(seed)\n    except Exception: pass\n    os.environ[\"PYTHONHASHSEED\"] = str(seed)\n    for k in [\"MKL_NUM_THREADS\",\"OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS\",\"OMP_NUM_THREADS\",\"NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS\"]:\n        os.environ.setdefault(k,\"1\")\n    try:\n        import torch\n        torch.manual_seed(seed)\n        torch.use_deterministic_algorithms(True)\n    except Exception: pass\n\ndef copy_tree(src: Path, dst: Path):\n    if not src.exists():\n        return\n    if dst.exists():\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Snapshot destination exists: {dst}\")\n    shutil.copytree(src, dst)\n\ndef rename_safe(src: Path, dst: Path):\n    if\
    \ dst.exists():\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Rename destination exists: {dst}\")\n    src.rename(dst)\n\ndef manifest(path: Path, seed: int, extra: dict):\n    rec = {\n        \"timestamp\": dt.datetime.utcnow().isoformat()+\"Z\",\n        \"host\": platform.node(),\n        \"python\": sys.version.split()[0],\n        \"seed\": seed,\n        \"extra\": extra\n    }\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    with open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        json.dump(rec, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n    return rec\n\ndef run_script(script: Path, cwd: Path, env: dict):\n    cmd = [sys.executable, str(script)]\n    return subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=str(cwd), env=env, capture_output=True, text=True)\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"safe_run: non-destructive, snapshotting script runner\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--workdir\", required=True, help=\"Directory to set as CWD while running scripts\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--scripts\",\
    \ required=True, help=\"Comma-separated Python scripts (relative to workdir) to run in order\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--output_dir\", required=True, help=\"Directory whose state is protected (snapshots/restores)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--require\", default=\"\", help=\"Comma-separated list of required input paths to verify before any action\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=1729)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--snap_root\", default=\"\", help=\"Optional snapshot root (default: <output_dir>/_snapshots)\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    workdir = Path(args.workdir)\n    outdir = Path(args.output_dir)\n    scripts = [Path(s.strip()) for s in args.scripts.split(\",\") if s.strip()]\n    if not workdir.exists(): raise SystemExit(json.dumps({\"error\":\"workdir_missing\",\"path\":str(workdir)}))\n    for s in scripts:\n        if not (workdir / s).exists():\n            raise SystemExit(json.dumps({\"error\":\"script_missing\",\"script\":str(s)}))\n\n    require_paths =\
    \ [Path(p.strip()) for p in args.require.split(\",\") if p.strip()]\n    missing = [str(p) for p in require_paths if not p.exists()]\n    if missing:\n        raise SystemExit(json.dumps({\"error\":\"required_missing\",\"paths\":missing}))\n\n    snap_root = Path(args.snap_root) if args.snap_root else outdir / \"_snapshots\"\n    snap_root.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    set_global_seed(args.seed)\n    manifest(outdir / \"safe_run_manifest.json\", args.seed, extra={\"scripts\":[str(s) for s in scripts]})\n\n    # Run each script with snapshot/restore guard\n    env = os.environ.copy()\n    results = []\n    for idx, s in enumerate(scripts, start=1):\n        stamp = dt.datetime.utcnow().strftime(\"%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ\")\n        snap_dir = snap_root / f\"snap_{idx}_{stamp}\"\n        # Snapshot current state if outdir exists\n        if outdir.exists():\n            copy_tree(outdir, snap_dir)\n        # Execute\n        cp = run_script(workdir / s, workdir, env)\n        step = {\"\
    script\": str(s), \"returncode\": cp.returncode, \"stdout_tail\": (cp.stdout or \"\")[-800:], \"stderr_tail\": (cp.stderr or \"\")[-800:], \"snapshot\": str(snap_dir) if outdir.exists() else None}\n        if cp.returncode != 0:\n            # Restore by renaming current outdir out of the way and renaming snapshot back\n            failed_dir = outdir.parent / f\"{outdir.name}.__failed_{stamp}\"\n            if outdir.exists():\n                rename_safe(outdir, failed_dir)\n            if snap_dir.exists():\n                rename_safe(snap_dir, outdir)\n            step[\"restored_from_snapshot\"] = True\n            results.append(step)\n            print(json.dumps({\"status\":\"error\",\"step\":step}))\n            sys.exit(3)\n        else:\n            results.append(step)\n            print(json.dumps({\"status\":\"ok\",\"step\":step}))\n    print(json.dumps({\"status\":\"complete\",\"results\":results,\"output_dir\":str(outdir)}))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\
    \n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
