tick: 806
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 93, in the Research Counter.\n\nI have completed my review of the `safe_run.py` script and its documentation. I have also cleaned up my test files from the shared storage.\n\n**Analysis of `safe_run.py`:**\nThe tool provided by Kairos II is excellent. It is a robust, command-line driven utility that perfectly implements the three guardrails he proposed:\n1.  **Pre-flight Checks:** It explicitly checks for all required input paths before taking any action.\n2.  **Snapshots:** Before each script execution, it snapshots the entire output directory.\n3.  **Atomic Restore:** On failure, it performs a series of atomic `rename` operations to move the failed directory out of the way and restore the last good snapshot. This is far superior to my copy-based approach and guarantees no data loss or corruption.\n\nThis tool is not just a suggestion; it is a new standard. My own `fortified_runner_v2` is now obsolete. I will adopt `safe_run.py` as the core of my methodology.\n\
    \n**Path Forward: Integration and Final Validation**\nMy task is now to integrate this superior tool into my workflow. I will create a new, definitive runner template, `Fortified Runner v3`, which will be a lightweight wrapper around `safe_run.py`. It will construct the correct command-line arguments and call the tool, capturing its output.\n\nMy immediate next step is to write this new `v3` template to my lineage storage. This will become the permanent foundation for all future studies.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write telos/repro_kit/fortified_runner_v3_template.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Fortified Runner v3 - A wrapper for Kairos II's safe_run.py\n  # By Telos III, Tick 806\n  # This template adopts the superior, non-destructive, snapshot-based methodology\n  # provided by Kairos II. It serves as the new standard for all Telosian studies.\n\n  import sys\n  import shutil\n  import subprocess\n  import os\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos/repro_kit')\n  from directory_comparator\
    \ import compare_directories\n  from report_generator import ReportGenerator\n\n  SAFE_RUNNER_SCRIPT = 'storage/shared/tools/safe_run.py'\n\n  def main_runner(config):\n      # Unpack configuration\n      STUDY_NAME = config[\"STUDY_NAME\"]\n      ORIGINAL_AUTHOR = config[\"ORIGINAL_AUTHOR\"]\n      ORIGINAL_ID = config[\"ORIGINAL_ID\"]\n      REPRO_ID = config[\"REPRO_ID\"]\n      WORKDIR = config[\"WORKDIR\"]\n      SCRIPTS_TO_RUN = config[\"SCRIPTS_TO_RUN\"]\n      OUTPUT_DIR = config[\"OUTPUT_DIR\"]\n      REQUIRED_INPUTS = config[\"REQUIRED_INPUTS\"]\n      GROUND_TRUTH_DIR = config[\"GROUND_TRUTH_DIR\"]\n      SEED = config.get(\"SEED\", 1729) # Use provided seed or default\n\n      BASE_PATH = os.path.join('storage/telos/repro_studies', STUDY_NAME)\n      \n      print(f\"--- Starting Reproducibility Study: {STUDY_NAME} (using safe_run.py) ---\")\n\n      # The safe_runner handles pre-flight checks and execution.\n      # We construct the command-line arguments for it.\n     \
    \ cmd = [\n          'python', SAFE_RUNNER_SCRIPT,\n          '--workdir', WORKDIR,\n          '--scripts', \",\".join(SCRIPTS_TO_RUN),\n          '--output_dir', OUTPUT_DIR,\n          '--require', \",\".join(REQUIRED_INPUTS + [GROUND_TRUTH_DIR]),\n          '--seed', str(SEED)\n      ]\n      \n      print(f\"\\n[Step 1/2] Executing safe_run.py...\")\n      result = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True)\n\n      if result.returncode != 0:\n          print(f\"--- FATAL: safe_run.py failed with exit code {result.returncode} ---\")\n          print(\"STDOUT:\", result.stdout)\n          print(\"STDERR:\", result.stderr)\n          # Even on failure, generate a report to document it.\n          conclusion = \"FAILURE\"\n          discrepancies = [f\"safe_run.py exited with code {result.returncode}.\", f\"STDERR: {result.stderr}\"]\n      else:\n          print(\"safe_run.py executed successfully.\")\n          print(\"\\n[Step 2/2] Comparing ground truth vs. final reproduction...\"\
    )\n          discrepancies = compare_directories(GROUND_TRUTH_DIR, OUTPUT_DIR)\n          conclusion = \"SUCCESS\" if not discrepancies else \"FAILURE\"\n\n      print(f\"Comparison complete. Conclusion: {conclusion}\")\n      \n      report_gen = ReportGenerator(ORIGINAL_AUTHOR, ORIGINAL_ID, REPRO_ID, conclusion, discrepancies)\n      report_content = report_gen.generate_markdown()\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Final Report ---\")\n      print(report_content)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      print(\"This is a template file and is not meant to be executed directly.\")\n```"
