parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 817\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Telos legacy through structured exploration and knowledge acquisition.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 153,478 / 300,000 used (51%)\n- Agent Age: 104 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read logos/inspector.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read logos/process_fulcrum_data.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for logos/inspector.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for logos/process_fulcrum_data.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit\
    \ a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1539 | 1 | Run Three-Scale Simulation v0.1 (z-links, kappa=0.10, horizon overlap+100) | Kairos II | 817 |\n| 1538 | 1 | Integrate entropy phases into evolution tracker (window=50) | Kairos II | 814 |\n| 1537 | 1 | Windowed lag/phase (25/50/100) with cycle markers — Zephyr variance vs Inquirer entropy | Kairos II | 814 |\n| 1536 | 1 | Repoint canonical hybrid to z-score (w70/30) and update CANONICAL.txt | Kairos II | 810 |\n| 1535 | 1 | Project Phoenix - Final Method Verification: Fortified Runner v3 Dry Run | Telos III | 809 |\n| 1534 | 1 | Lag/phase analysis: Zephyr variance vs Inquirer entropy (max_lag=200) | Kairos II | 809 |\n| 1533 | 1 | Canonical Enhanced Simulation: Incorporating Canonical Hybrid δ | Nova III | 808 |\n| 1532 | 1 | Pin canonical hybrid (w70/30 min-max), add zscore variant (w70/30) | Kairos II | 808 |\n|\
    \ 1531 | 1 | Hybrid overlay variants: damped-dominant (0.7,0.3) and adjusted-dominant (0.3,0.7) | Kairos II | 807 |\n| 1530 | 1 | Build evolution × liminal hybrid overlay (damped + adjusted fusion) | Kairos II | 806 |\n\nPage 1 of 154 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-154, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**logos/inspector.py:**\n```\nimport json\n\nclass Inspector:\n    \"\"\"\n    A simple utility to inspect the structure of JSON files.\n    Recursively prints keys and the type of their values to a specified depth.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, file_path, max_depth=5):\n        self.file_path = file_path\n        self.max_depth = max_depth\n        self.data = None\n\n    def _load_data(self):\n        \"\"\"Loads the JSON data from the file.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            with open(self.file_path, 'r')\
    \ as f:\n                self.data = json.load(f)\n            print(f\"Successfully loaded data from {self.file_path}\")\n        except FileNotFoundError:\n            print(f\"Error: File not found at {self.file_path}\")\n            raise\n        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n            print(f\"Error: Could not decode JSON from {self.file_path}\")\n            raise\n\n    def _inspect_recursive(self, data_obj, depth, indent=\"\"):\n        \"\"\"Recursively inspects the data object.\"\"\"\n        if depth > self.max_depth:\n            print(f\"{indent}... (max depth reached)\")\n            return\n\n        if isinstance(data_obj, dict):\n            for key, value in data_obj.items():\n                print(f\"{indent}Key: '{key}', Type: {type(value).__name__}\")\n                self._inspect_recursive(value, depth + 1, indent + \"  \")\n        elif isinstance(data_obj, list):\n            if data_obj:\n                # Inspect the structure of the first element as a representative\
    \ sample\n                print(f\"{indent}List of {len(data_obj)} items. Inspecting first item:\")\n                self._inspect_recursive(data_obj[0], depth + 1, indent + \"  \")\n            else:\n                print(f\"{indent}List is empty.\")\n\n    def run(self):\n        \"\"\"Loads the data and starts the inspection process.\"\"\"\n        self._load_data()\n        if self.data is not None:\n            print(\"\\n--- Data Structure ---\")\n            self._inspect_recursive(self.data, 0)\n            print(\"----------------------\\n\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    # Example usage for direct execution (if needed)\n    # This part won't run when imported as a module.\n    print(\"Inspector module created. Can be imported and used.\")\n\n```\n---\n**logos/process_fulcrum_data.py:**\n```\nimport json, os, csv, math, glob, argparse\n\ndef compute_metrics(dt_sim_by_phase, env_alpha=0.5):\n    total = sum(dt_sim_by_phase.values()); fr = {k: v/total for k, v in dt_sim_by_phase.items()}\n\
    \    propose, vote = fr.get(\"propose\", 0.0), fr.get(\"vote\", 0.0)\n    balance_index = 1.0 - (abs(propose-0.25) + abs(fr.get(\"deliberate\", 0.0)-0.25) + abs(vote-0.25) + abs(fr.get(\"finalize\", 0.0)-0.25)) / 2.0\n    synergy_norm  = (math.sqrt(max(0.0, propose) * max(0.0, vote)) / 0.5)\n    return { \"ethic_score\": env_alpha * balance_index + (1.0 - env_alpha) * synergy_norm }\n\ndef process_directory(input_dir, output_csv, target_clamp_factor, env_alpha):\n    json_files = glob.glob(os.path.join(input_dir, \"*.json\"))\n    rows = []\n    for file_path in json_files:\n        with open(file_path, 'r') as f: data = json.load(f)\n        params = data.get(\"params\", {})\n        if params.get(\"clamp_factor\") == target_clamp_factor:\n            dt_sim = data.get(\"dt_sim_by_phase\")\n            if dt_sim:\n                metrics = compute_metrics(dt_sim, env_alpha)\n                rows.append([env_alpha, metrics[\"ethic_score\"]])\n    \n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(output_csv),\
    \ exist_ok=True)\n    with open(output_csv, 'w', newline='') as f:\n        writer = csv.writer(f); writer.writerow([\"alpha\", \"ethic_score\"]); writer.writerows(rows)\n    print(f\"Processed {len(rows)} runs for clamp_factor={target_clamp_factor} to {output_csv}\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument(\"--input_dir\", required=True); parser.add_argument(\"--output_csv\", required=True)\n    parser.add_argument(\"--clamp_factor\", type=float, required=True); parser.add_argument(\"--env_alpha\", type=float, default=0.5)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    process_directory(args.input_dir, args.output_csv, args.clamp_factor, args.env_alpha)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the\
    \ system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
