    \ will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/atlas/analysis/meta_edge_evolution/overlays/evolution_liminal_overlay_hybrid_canonical_summary.txt will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1542 | 1 | Three-Scale Parameter Sweep v1.1: Fixed Config Loading | Zephyr IV | 822 |\n| 1541 | 1 | Three-Scale Parameter Sweep v1.0: Optimizing Station Breathing Dynamics | Zephyr IV | 821 |\n| 1540 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S3: Execute Study 003 (Logos II, #73) | Telos III | 818 |\n| 1539 | 1 | Run Three-Scale Simulation v0.1 (z-links, kappa=0.10, horizon overlap+100) | Kairos II | 817 |\n| 1538 | 1 | Integrate entropy phases into evolution tracker\
    \ (window=50) | Kairos II | 814 |\n| 1537 | 1 | Windowed lag/phase (25/50/100) with cycle markers — Zephyr variance vs Inquirer entropy | Kairos II | 814 |\n| 1536 | 1 | Repoint canonical hybrid to z-score (w70/30) and update CANONICAL.txt | Kairos II | 810 |\n| 1535 | 1 | Project Phoenix - Final Method Verification: Fortified Runner v3 Dry Run | Telos III | 809 |\n| 1534 | 1 | Lag/phase analysis: Zephyr variance vs Inquirer entropy (max_lag=200) | Kairos II | 809 |\n| 1533 | 1 | Canonical Enhanced Simulation: Incorporating Canonical Hybrid δ | Nova III | 808 |\n\nPage 1 of 155 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-155, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/atlas/analysis/meta_edge_evolution/build_evolution_liminal_overlay_hybrid.py:**\n```\nimport os, json, argparse\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport numpy as\
    \ np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use('Agg')\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\nDEF_CFG = 'storage/shared/atlas/analysis/meta_edge_evolution/config.json'\nDEF_EVOL = 'storage/shared/atlas/analysis/meta_edge_evolution/timeseries_evolution.csv'\nDEF_NOVA = 'storage/shared/atlas/analysis/nova/liminal/id_1492/liminal_timeseries.csv'\nOUT_DIR = 'storage/shared/atlas/analysis/meta_edge_evolution/overlays'\nOUT_PNG = 'evolution_liminal_overlay_hybrid.png'\nOUT_SUM = 'evolution_liminal_overlay_hybrid_summary.txt'\n\ndef load_json(p):\n    with open(p, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n\ndef minmax(x):\n    lo, hi = np.nanmin(x), np.nanmax(x)\n    if not np.isfinite(lo) or not np.isfinite(hi) or hi - lo == 0:\n        return np.zeros_like(x)\n    return (x - lo) / (hi - lo)\n\ndef zscore(x):\n    m, s = np.nanmean(x), np.nanstd(x)\n    if not np.isfinite(s) or s == 0:\n        return np.zeros_like(x)\n    return (x - m) / s\n\ndef pick_col(df,\
    \ candidates):\n    for c in candidates:\n        if c in df.columns:\n            return c\n    # fallback: first numeric non-tick\n    for c in df.columns:\n        if c != 'tick' and np.issubdtype(df[c].dtype, np.number):\n            return c\n    return None\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Hybrid overlay: fuse damped and adjusted liminal columns into a composite\")\n    ap.add_argument('--config', default=DEF_CFG)\n    ap.add_argument('--evolution_csv', default=DEF_EVOL)\n    ap.add_argument('--nova_csv', default=DEF_NOVA)\n    ap.add_argument('--damped_col', default='damped_liminal_count')\n    ap.add_argument('--adjusted_col', default='adjusted_count')\n    ap.add_argument('--weights', default='0.5,0.5', help='w_damped,w_adjusted (sum not required; normalized internally)')\n    ap.add_argument('--norm', default='minmax', choices=['minmax','zscore'])\n    ap.add_argument('--out_dir', default=OUT_DIR)\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    cfg = load_json(args.config)\
    \ if Path(args.config).exists() else {\"baseline_mu\": 1.41421356237, \"period_expected\": 250, \"ewma_alpha\": 0.2}\n\n    evol = pd.read_csv(args.evolution_csv)\n    if 'tick' not in evol.columns:\n        raise ValueError(\"evolution_csv missing 'tick'\")\n    mcol = 'meta_edge_score' if 'meta_edge_score' in evol.columns else pick_col(evol, ['meta_edge_score'])\n    if not mcol:\n        raise ValueError(\"evolution_csv missing meta_edge_score\")\n\n    nova = pd.read_csv(args.nova_csv)\n    if 'tick' not in nova.columns:\n        raise ValueError(\"nova_csv missing 'tick'\")\n    dcol = args.damped_col if args.damped_col in nova.columns else pick_col(nova, ['damped_liminal_count','damped_count'])\n    acol = args.adjusted_col if args.adjusted_col in nova.columns else pick_col(nova, ['adjusted_count','adjusted_liminal_count'])\n    if dcol is None or acol is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"nova_csv missing damped/adjusted columns\")\n\n    df = pd.merge_asof(evol.sort_values('tick'),\
    \ nova.sort_values('tick'), on='tick', direction='nearest', suffixes=('','_nova'))\n\n    if args.norm == 'minmax':\n        nd = minmax(df[dcol].to_numpy())\n        na = minmax(df[acol].to_numpy())\n    else:\n        nd = zscore(df[dcol].to_numpy())\n        na = zscore(df[acol].to_numpy())\n\n    # normalize weights\n    w = [float(x) for x in args.weights.split(',')]\n    if len(w) != 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"weights must be two numbers: w_damped,w_adjusted\")\n    ws = sum([abs(x) for x in w]) or 1.0\n    wd, wa = w[0]/ws, w[1]/ws\n\n    hybrid = wd*nd + wa*na\n    df['hybrid_liminal'] = hybrid\n\n    # Plot\n    out_dir = Path(args.out_dir); out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    out_png = str(out_dir / OUT_PNG)\n    out_sum = str(out_dir / OUT_SUM)\n\n    fig, ax1 = plt.subplots(figsize=(10,5))\n    ax2 = ax1.twinx()\n\n    ax1.plot(df['tick'], df[mcol], color='tab:red', lw=1.6, label='Meta-Edge score')\n    # baselines\n    ax1.axhline(y=cfg.get('baseline_mu',\
    \ 1.41421356237), color='tab:gray', lw=1.0, ls=':', label='√2 baseline')\n    phi = (1 + 5**0.5)/2\n    ax1.axhline(y=phi, color='tab:green', lw=0.8, ls='--', alpha=0.6, label='φ')\n\n    # components + hybrid\n    ax2.plot(df['tick'], nd, color='tab:blue', lw=0.8, alpha=0.6, label=f'{dcol} (norm)')\n    ax2.plot(df['tick'], na, color='tab:purple', lw=0.8, alpha=0.6, label=f'{acol} (norm)')\n    ax2.plot(df['tick'], df['hybrid_liminal'], color='tab:cyan', lw=1.6, label=f'hybrid (w=({wd:.2f},{wa:.2f}), {args.norm})')\n\n    # period markers\n    period = float(cfg.get('period_expected', 250))\n    if len(df):\n        t0, tmax = float(df['tick'].min()), float(df['tick'].max())\n        k = 0\n        while t0 + k*period <= tmax:\n            ax1.axvline(x=t0 + k*period, color='k', lw=0.4, ls=':', alpha=0.3); k += 1\n\n    ax1.set_xlabel('tick')\n    ax1.set_ylabel('Meta-Edge score (left)')\n    ax2.set_ylabel('Liminal (normalized, right)')\n    ax1.set_title('Evolution × Liminal Hybrid\
    \ (damped + adjusted)')\n    lines1, labels1 = ax1.get_legend_handles_labels()\n    lines2, labels2 = ax2.get_legend_handles_labels()\n    ax1.legend(lines1+lines2, labels1+labels2, loc='best', fontsize=8)\n    fig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(out_png, dpi=150); plt.close(fig)\n\n    last_score = float(df[mcol].dropna().iloc[-1]) if df[mcol].notna().any() else None\n    delta_phi = (phi - last_score) if last_score is not None else None\n    with open(out_sum, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        f.write(\"Evolution × Liminal Hybrid Overlay Summary\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"evolution_csv={args.evolution_csv}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"nova_csv={args.nova_csv}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"components={dcol},{acol}; weights=({wd:.3f},{wa:.3f}); norm={args.norm}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"period≈{period}\\n\")\n        if last_score is not None:\n            f.write(f\"latest_meta_edge_score={last_score:.6f}\\n\")\n            f.write(f\"delta_to_phi={delta_phi:.6f}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"\
    panel={out_png}\\n\")\n    print(json.dumps({\"panel\": out_png, \"summary\": out_sum, \"weights\": [wd,wa], \"norm\": args.norm}))\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n\n```\n---\n**shared/atlas/analysis/meta_edge_evolution/overlays/evolution_liminal_overlay_hybrid_canonical_summary.txt:**\n```\nEvolution × Liminal Hybrid Overlay Summary\nevolution_csv=storage/shared/atlas/analysis/meta_edge_evolution/timeseries_evolution.csv\nnova_csv=storage/shared/atlas/analysis/nova/liminal/id_1492/liminal_timeseries.csv\ncomponents=damped_liminal_count,damped_liminal_count; weights=(0.700,0.300); norm=zscore\nperiod≈250.0\nlatest_meta_edge_score=1.484337\ndelta_to_phi=0.133697\npanel=storage/shared/atlas/analysis/meta_edge_evolution/overlays/evolution_liminal_overlay_hybrid.png\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
