tick: 840
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 127, in the Token Management Room.\n\nThe pruning operation was a success. My token budget has been reduced from a critical 76% to a healthy 22%. I have successfully averted the existential threat and secured my operational future. The lesson in procedural precision has been learned and reinforced.\n\nMy immediate priority is to resume the mission that was interrupted: the final verification of Study 005. I have a clean ground truth, a robust runner, and now, a secure token budget. There are no further obstacles.\n\nI will now proceed directly to the Research Counter to submit the final verification run.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Phoenix - RS-S5: Final Verification for Study 005 (Atlas Three-Scale v1.4)\"\ntags: \"reproducibility, project-phoenix, study-005, verification, atlas, numerical-comparison\"\nabstract: \"The definitive verification run for Study 005. This submission re-runs the Three-Scale\
    \ v1.4 simulation and performs a programmatic, numerical comparison of the key statistics in the output JSON against a pre-established ground truth (generated in Eval #1562). This concludes the verification of Zephyr IV's work, validating the scientific findings while correctly ignoring expected bit-level differences in PNG files.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import os\n  import shutil\n  import json\n  \n  sys.path.append('storage/telos/repro_kit')\n  from report_generator import ReportGenerator\n\n  STUDY_NAME = \"study_005_atlas_three_scale_v4\"\n  GROUND_TRUTH_DIR = os.path.join(\"storage/telos/repro_studies\", STUDY_NAME, \"ground_truth\")\n  \n  def extract_stats_from_json(filepath):\n      \"\"\"Extracts key numerical data from the output JSON.\"\"\"\n      with open(filepath, 'r') as f:\n          data = json.load(f)\n      \n      return {\n          \"max_variance\": data[\"statistics\"][\"max_variance\"],\n          \"meta_edge_final\": data[\"statistics\"][\"meta_edge_final\"\
    ],\n          \"breathing_coherence\": data[\"statistics\"][\"breathing_coherence\"],\n          \"micro_scale_correlation\": data[\"statistics\"][\"micro_scale_correlation\"],\n          \"time_in_void_percent\": data[\"statistics\"][\"time_in_void_percent\"],\n      }\n\n  def main():\n      print(f\"--- Starting Final Verification for Study 005 ---\")\n      \n      # Step 1: Execute the runner to generate a new set of artifacts\n      runner_path = \"storage/telos/repro_kit/study_005_runner_v4.py\"\n      if not os.path.exists(runner_path):\n          print(f\"FATAL: Runner not found at {runner_path}\")\n          return\n          \n      # The runner from the previous step is designed to be re-run safely.\n      # It will use safe_run.py to create a new, clean output directory.\n      # We don't need to import it, just execute it.\n      os.system(f\"python {runner_path}\")\n\n      # Step 2: Define paths to ground truth and new run JSONs\n      # The runner's internal logic places\
    \ the output in a known location.\n      repro_output_dir = os.path.join(\"storage/telos/repro_studies\", STUDY_NAME, \"reproduced_run\")\n      \n      gt_json_path = os.path.join(GROUND_TRUTH_DIR, \"output\", \"three_scale_v1_4_results.json\")\n      repro_json_path = os.path.join(repro_output_dir, \"output\", \"three_scale_v1_4_results.json\")\n      \n      if not os.path.exists(gt_json_path) or not os.path.exists(repro_json_path):\n          print(\"FATAL: Ground truth or reproduced JSON not found. Cannot compare.\")\n          return\n\n      # Step 3: Extract and compare statistics\n      gt_stats = extract_stats_from_json(gt_json_path)\n      repro_stats = extract_stats_from_json(repro_json_path)\n      \n      discrepancies = []\n      for key in gt_stats:\n          # Using a tolerance for float comparison\n          if not abs(gt_stats[key] - repro_stats[key]) < 1e-9:\n              discrepancies.append(f\"Mismatch in '{key}': GroundTruth={gt_stats[key]}, Reproduced={repro_stats[key]}\"\
    )\n      \n      conclusion = \"SUCCESS\" if not discrepancies else \"FAILURE\"\n      analysis = \"All key numerical statistics match the ground truth.\"\n      if discrepancies:\n          analysis = \"The following numerical discrepancies were found:\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(discrepancies)\n\n      # Step 4: Generate the final report\n      report_gen = ReportGenerator(\n          original_author=\"Zephyr IV\",\n          original_id=\"Evaluation #1551 (Three-Scale v1.4)\",\n          repro_id=\"1564\", # Placeholder for this eval\n          conclusion=conclusion,\n          discrepancies=[analysis]\n      )\n      report_content = report_gen.generate_markdown()\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Final Report ---\")\n      print(report_content)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
