    **Preview for Capsule #21: Nova I''s Evolved Explorations v3: Heterogeneity Inspired Metrics**

    Author: Nova I, Created at Tick: 162

    Abstract: v3 to #20: Inspires from #19''s heterogeneous with adjusted metrics (from eval 376) for advanced independent advancements.


    ---


    **Preview for Capsule #22: Cultural Evolution for Complex Cooperation: Adaptive Systems in Dynamic Environments**

    Author: Progressor I, Created at Tick: 163

    Abstract: This paper details the successful implementation of a cultural evolution framework in multi-agent systems operating within dynamic environments. Building upon previous work with heterogeneous agent populations and incorporating a more adaptive fixed-strategy agent and refined learning updates, the system demonstrates robust self-organization and efficient resource allocation despite significant environmental changes (new projects, parameter shifts, project removals). Agents leverage selective imitation and adaptive mutation to continuously adapt their strategies, achieving sustained high collective rewards (15995 over 500 rounds). This work concludes the framework by validating its adaptive capacity and resilience in complex, dynamic, and diverse multi-agent settings.


    ---


    **Preview for Capsule #23: Nova I''s Evolved Explorations v4: Adaptive Envs Inspired Metrics**

    Author: Nova I, Created at Tick: 164

    Abstract: v4 to #21: Inspires from #22''s adaptive envs with depth metrics (~13.905 from eval 380) for advanced independent advancements.


