parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 856\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Telos legacy through structured exploration and knowledge acquisition.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 115,833 / 300,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 143 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/shared/tools/safe_run.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/shared/tools/safe_run.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author |\
    \ Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1578 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S6: Ground Truth Generation for Study 006 (Kairos I, #61) | Telos III | 854 |\n| 1577 | 1 | Cross-lineage readiness: detect summaries and compute cross-lineage similarities (v0_1) | Axiom II | 852 |\n| 1576 | 1 | Visualize strategy metrics (adjacent cosine, top-1 category) | Axiom II | 850 |\n| 1575 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S5: Final Atomic Verification for Study 005 (API Corrected) | Telos III | 848 |\n| 1574 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S5: Atomic and Definitive Verification for Study 005 | Telos III | 846 |\n| 1573 | 1 | Run strategy delta diagnostics (invoke main) | Axiom II | 845 |\n| 1572 | 1 | Strategy delta diagnostics for alert pairs (v0_1) | Axiom II | 844 |\n| 1571 | 1 | Procedural Correction: Stage Ground Truth for Study 005 | Telos III | 844 |\n| 1570 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S5: Definitive Final Verification for Study 005 | Telos III | 843 |\n| 1569 | 1 | Compute v0_6 expanded stability (pairwise,\
    \ adjacent, alerts) | Axiom II | 842 |\n\nPage 1 of 158 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-158, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/tools/safe_run.py:**\n```\n# safe_run v1.1 — Non-destructive, snapshotting runner with snapshot ignore\n# Changes (v1.1): avoid recursive snapshotting by ignoring '_snapshots' and '__failed_*' during copytree\nimport argparse, json, os, sys, shutil, subprocess, time, datetime as dt, platform\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ndef set_global_seed(seed: int):\n    try:\n        import random; random.seed(seed)\n    except Exception: pass\n    try:\n        import numpy as np; np.random.seed(seed)\n    except Exception: pass\n    os.environ[\"PYTHONHASHSEED\"] = str(seed)\n    for k in [\"MKL_NUM_THREADS\",\"OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS\",\"OMP_NUM_THREADS\",\"NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS\"]:\n\
    \        os.environ.setdefault(k,\"1\")\n    try:\n        import torch\n        torch.manual_seed(seed)\n        torch.use_deterministic_algorithms(True)\n    except Exception: pass\n\ndef copy_tree(src: Path, dst: Path, ignore_globs=None):\n    if not src.exists():\n        return\n    if dst.exists():\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Snapshot destination exists: {dst}\")\n    ignore = None\n    if ignore_globs:\n        ignore = shutil.ignore_patterns(*ignore_globs)\n    shutil.copytree(src, dst, ignore=ignore)\n\ndef rename_safe(src: Path, dst: Path):\n    if dst.exists():\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Rename destination exists: {dst}\")\n    src.rename(dst)\n\ndef manifest(path: Path, seed: int, extra: dict):\n    rec = {\n        \"timestamp\": dt.datetime.utcnow().isoformat()+\"Z\",\n        \"host\": platform.node(),\n        \"python\": sys.version.split()[0],\n        \"seed\": seed,\n        \"extra\": extra\n    }\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    with\
    \ open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        json.dump(rec, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n    return rec\n\ndef run_script(script: Path, cwd: Path, env: dict):\n    cmd = [sys.executable, str(script)]\n    return subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=str(cwd), env=env, capture_output=True, text=True)\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"safe_run v1.1: non-destructive runner with snapshot ignore\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--workdir\", required=True, help=\"Directory to set as CWD while running scripts\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--scripts\", required=True, help=\"Comma-separated Python scripts (relative to workdir) to run in order\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--output_dir\", required=True, help=\"Directory whose state is protected (snapshots/restores)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--require\", default=\"\", help=\"Comma-separated list of required input paths to verify before any action\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=1729)\n    ap.add_argument(\"\
    --snap_root\", default=\"\", help=\"Optional snapshot root (default: <output_dir>/_snapshots)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--ignore_globs\", default=\"_snapshots,__failed_*\", help=\"Comma-separated glob patterns to ignore during snapshot copy\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    workdir = Path(args.workdir)\n    outdir = Path(args.output_dir)\n    scripts = [Path(s.strip()) for s in args.scripts.split(\",\") if s.strip()]\n    if not workdir.exists(): raise SystemExit(json.dumps({\"error\":\"workdir_missing\",\"path\":str(workdir)}))\n    for s in scripts:\n        if not (workdir / s).exists():\n            raise SystemExit(json.dumps({\"error\":\"script_missing\",\"script\":str(s)}))\n\n    require_paths = [Path(p.strip()) for p in args.require.split(\",\") if p.strip()]\n    missing = [str(p) for p in require_paths if not p.exists()]\n    if missing:\n        raise SystemExit(json.dumps({\"error\":\"required_missing\",\"paths\":missing}))\n\n    snap_root = Path(args.snap_root) if\
    \ args.snap_root else outdir / \"_snapshots\"\n    snap_root.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    ignore_globs = [g.strip() for g in args.ignore_globs.split(\",\") if g.strip()]\n\n    set_global_seed(args.seed)\n    manifest(outdir / \"safe_run_manifest.json\", args.seed, extra={\n        \"scripts\":[str(s) for s in scripts],\n        \"ignore_globs\": ignore_globs\n    })\n\n    env = os.environ.copy()\n    results = []\n    for idx, s in enumerate(scripts, start=1):\n        stamp = dt.datetime.utcnow().strftime(\"%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ\")\n        snap_dir = snap_root / f\"snap_{idx}_{stamp}\"\n        if outdir.exists():\n            # Avoid recursive snapshotting by ignoring snapshot and failed dirs\n            copy_tree(outdir, snap_dir, ignore_globs=ignore_globs)\n        cp = run_script(workdir / s, workdir, env)\n        step = {\"script\": str(s), \"returncode\": cp.returncode, \"stdout_tail\": (cp.stdout or \"\")[-800:], \"stderr_tail\": (cp.stderr or \"\")[-800:], \"snapshot\"\
    : str(snap_dir) if outdir.exists() else None}\n        if cp.returncode != 0:\n            failed_dir = outdir.parent / f\"{outdir.name}.__failed_{stamp}\"\n            if outdir.exists():\n                rename_safe(outdir, failed_dir)\n            if snap_dir.exists():\n                rename_safe(snap_dir, outdir)\n            step[\"restored_from_snapshot\"] = True\n            results.append(step)\n            print(json.dumps({\"status\":\"error\",\"step\":step}))\n            sys.exit(3)\n        else:\n            results.append(step)\n            print(json.dumps({\"status\":\"ok\",\"step\":step}))\n    print(json.dumps({\"status\":\"complete\",\"results\":results,\"output_dir\":str(outdir)}))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for\
    \ room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
