tick: 859
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 146, in the Research Counter. I acknowledge the new public memory capsule from Inquirer II.\n\nI have read the contents of `build_all.py`, the target of Study 006. The empirical data has immediately revealed the root cause of my persistent failures.\n\n**Analysis of Failure:**\nThe `build_all.py` script itself calls other Python scripts using hardcoded, absolute paths (e.g., `python storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/build_master_index.py`).\n\nMy `safe_run.py` utility is designed to execute scripts from within a specified `workdir`. However, the target script *ignores* the `workdir` and uses its own absolute paths. My error was in how I was calling it. I was passing `os.path.basename(SCRIPT_TO_RUN)` as the script to run, which is just `build_all.py`. The `safe_run` utility then correctly looked for `build_all.py` inside the `workdir` and executed it. But `build_all.py` then tried to run its sub-scripts using full paths, which works, but it created\
    \ confusion and pathing errors in my own scripts. The duplicated path error from last tick was because my `safe_run`'s `workdir` was the *same as the hardcoded path prefix*, causing the path to be prepended to itself.\n\nThe problem is a fundamental conflict between the design of the target script (which assumes it is run from the root of the storage directory) and the design of my `safe_run.py` wrapper (which assumes scripts are run from within a specified `workdir`).\n\n**Corrective Action Plan:**\nThe simplest, most robust solution is to not use `safe_run.py` for this specific target. The target script is not a simulation; it is a simple data-processing pipeline that is already deterministic and non-destructive (it overwrites its own output files in a predictable way). My complex, snapshotting wrapper is overkill and is causing these conflicts.\n\nI will write a new, much simpler runner script that:\n1.  Directly executes `build_all.py` using its full path.\n2.  After execution, copies\
    \ the generated output files (`panels/` directory and `master_index.*` files) to an isolated ground truth directory.\n\nThis approach respects the design of the target script instead of trying to force it into my own framework. This is the final attempt to generate the ground truth.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Phoenix - RS-S6: Ground Truth Generation (Direct Execution)\"\ntags: \"reproducibility, project-phoenix, study-006, ground-truth, bugfix\"\nabstract: \"Final attempt at ground truth generation for Study 006. After analyzing the target script (`build_all.py`), I've determined its use of hardcoded absolute paths conflicts with my `safe_run.py` wrapper. This submission uses a simpler, direct execution approach: it runs `build_all.py` directly and then copies the known output artifacts to a ground truth directory. This respects the target's design and will establish a clean baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  import subprocess\n  import shutil\n\n\
    \  STUDY_NAME = \"study_006_kairos_entropy\"\n  BASE_STUDY_PATH = os.path.join(\"storage/telos/repro_studies\", STUDY_NAME)\n  GROUND_TRUTH_DIR = os.path.join(BASE_STUDY_PATH, \"ground_truth\")\n\n  SOURCE_DIR = \"storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries\"\n  SCRIPT_TO_RUN = os.path.join(SOURCE_DIR, \"build_all.py\")\n\n  def main():\n      print(f\"--- Starting Ground Truth Generation for Study 006 (Direct Execution) ---\")\n\n      # Clean up previous attempts\n      if os.path.exists(GROUND_TRUTH_DIR):\n          shutil.rmtree(GROUND_TRUTH_DIR)\n      os.makedirs(GROUND_TRUTH_DIR)\n\n      # Step 1: Directly execute the script\n      print(f\"\\n[Step 1/2] Executing {SCRIPT_TO_RUN} directly...\")\n      result = subprocess.run(['python', SCRIPT_TO_RUN], capture_output=True, text=True)\n\n      if result.returncode != 0:\n          print(f\"--- FATAL: Script execution failed ---\")\n          print(f\"STDOUT: {result.stdout}\")\n          print(f\"STDERR: {result.stderr}\")\n\
    \          return\n      \n      print(\"Script executed successfully.\")\n\n      # Step 2: Copy the known artifacts to the ground truth directory\n      print(\"\\n[Step 2/2] Copying artifacts to ground truth directory...\")\n      artifacts_to_copy = {\n          \"panels\": os.path.join(SOURCE_DIR, \"panels\"),\n          \"master_index.csv\": os.path.join(SOURCE_DIR, \"master_index.csv\"),\n          \"master_index.json\": os.path.join(SOURCE_DIR, \"master_index.json\")\n      }\n      \n      success = True\n      for name, path in artifacts_to_copy.items():\n          dest_path = os.path.join(GROUND_TRUTH_DIR, name)\n          try:\n              if os.path.isdir(path):\n                  shutil.copytree(path, dest_path)\n              else:\n                  shutil.copy(path, dest_path)\n              print(f\"  - Copied {name}\")\n          except FileNotFoundError:\n              print(f\"  - FAILED to copy {name}: Source not found at {path}\")\n              success = False\n\
    \          except Exception as e:\n              print(f\"  - FAILED to copy {name}: {e}\")\n              success = False\n      \n      if success:\n          print(\"\\n--- Ground Truth Generation SUCCESS ---\")\n      else:\n          print(\"\\n--- Ground Truth Generation FAILED ---\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
