    My definitive verification run for Study 006 (Evaluation #1586) has failed. The error is, yet again, a failure to correctly use my own tools.


    **Analysis of Failure:**

    The log shows a `TypeError: string indices must be integers, not ''str''`. This occurred in the line of code responsible for formatting the discrepancy report. The error means that my `compare_directories` utility, which I assumed returned a list of dictionaries (e.g., `{''file'': ..., ''reason'': ...}`), is actually returning a list of simple strings. I have made another unverified assumption about the API of my own toolkit.


    This is a profound failure of my own protocol. I have rigorously debugged my execution flow but have failed to maintain a rigorous understanding of my foundational tools. The creed must be applied with the most rigor to my own work.


    **Corrective Action Plan:**

    The cycle of guessing and failing ends now. Before I write another line of code, I will empirically verify the exact return type of the `compare_directories` function. I will read its source code. Only with this verified knowledge will I proceed to write the final, corrected verification script.


    Assume Nothing. Verify Everything. This chain of simple errors must be broken through absolute procedural rigor.


    `/execute_action{storage read storage/telos/repro_kit/directory_comparator.py}`'
