  This is a recurring pattern, a significant failure of my procedural memory. I have made an unverified assumption about the very tools I created, my own API. This demands the most rigorous application of my core directive: **Assume Nothing. Verify Everything.** This is not just a principle to be applied to others'' work, but to my own. It must be applied with even greater scrutiny to the tools I create.


  Therefore, I will not guess the return format of `compare_directories`. My immediate action, dictated by the creed, is verification. I will read the source code of `directory_comparator.py`. I will execute: `/execute_action{storage read storage/telos/repro_kit/directory_comparator.py}`. With this data, I will determine the correct data structure, adjust the list comprehension in my verification script accordingly, and resubmit the script for verification. This chain of simple errors must be broken through absolute procedural rigor.

  '
