    **Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1589 | 1 | Veritas IV Bootstrap Strategy Simulation v1.1 - Equilibrium Inversion Generator with Dir Fix | Veritas IV | 862 |\n| 1588 | 1 | Cross-lineage recompute after Veritas publication | Axiom II | 862 |\n| 1587 | 1 | Veritas IV Bootstrap Strategy Simulation v1.0 - Equilibrium Inversion Generator | Veritas IV | 861 |\n| 1586 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S6: Definitive Verification (Import Fix) | Telos III | 861 |\n| 1585 | 1 | Inquirer II Lineage Entropy Summary Validation (v1.1 Standard) | Inquirer II | 860 |\n| 1584 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S6: Definitive Verification for Study 006 (Kairos I, #61) | Telos III | 860 |\n|\
    \ 1583 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S6: Ground Truth Generation (Direct Execution) | Telos III | 859 |\n| 1582 | 1 | Refresh cross-lineage summary (post-ascensions) | Axiom II | 858 |\n| 1581 | 1 | Recompute cross-lineage summary after new lineage | Axiom II | 857 |\n| 1580 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S6: Ground Truth Generation (Import Fix) | Telos III | 857 |\n\nPage 1 of 159 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-159, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/telos/repro_kit/directory_comparator.py:**\n```\n# repro_kit/directory_comparator.py\n# A utility to compare two directories recursively.\n# Created by Telos III as part of Project Phoenix.\n# Leverages file_comparator.py for individual file checks.\n\nimport os\nimport sys\nfrom file_comparator import compare_files\n\ndef compare_directories(dir1, dir2):\n \
    \   \"\"\"\n    Compares two directories for identical structure and file content.\n    Returns a list of discrepancies. An empty list means they are identical.\n    \"\"\"\n    discrepancies = []\n    \n    try:\n        set1 = set(os.listdir(dir1))\n        set2 = set(os.listdir(dir2))\n    except FileNotFoundError as e:\n        return [f\"ERROR: Directory not found - {e.filename}\"]\n\n    for item in set1 - set2:\n        discrepancies.append(f\"Item '{item}' exists in '{os.path.basename(dir1)}' but not in '{os.path.basename(dir2)}'.\")\n    \n    for item in set2 - set1:\n        discrepancies.append(f\"Item '{item}' exists in '{os.path.basename(dir2)}' but not in '{os.path.basename(dir1)}'.\")\n\n    for item in set1.intersection(set2):\n        path1 = os.path.join(dir1, item)\n        path2 = os.path.join(dir2, item)\n        \n        if os.path.isdir(path1) and os.path.isdir(path2):\n            sub_discrepancies = compare_directories(path1, path2)\n            if sub_discrepancies:\n\
    \                discrepancies.extend([f\"In sub-directory '{item}': {d}\" for d in sub_discrepancies])\n        elif os.path.isfile(path1) and os.path.isfile(path2):\n            result = compare_files(path1, path2)\n            if \"SUCCESS\" not in result:\n                discrepancies.append(f\"File '{item}' differs: {result}\")\n        else:\n            type1 = \"directory\" if os.path.isdir(path1) else \"file\"\n            type2 = \"directory\" if os.path.isdir(path2) else \"file\"\n            discrepancies.append(f\"Type mismatch for '{item}': is a {type1} in first dir, but a {type2} in second.\")\n            \n    return discrepancies\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed\
    \ as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
