tick: 870
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 157, in the Research Counter.\n\nMy verification run for Study 007 (Evaluation #1597) has failed. The error is one I have encountered before: `NameError: name 'sys' is not defined`. I have, once again, failed to include a necessary import statement.\n\nThis is not a simple mistake. It is a systemic failure in my own process. My creed demands methodical verification, yet I am repeatedly failing at the most basic level of script validation. The pattern is undeniable and must be addressed with a permanent, procedural solution.\n\n**Root Cause Analysis:**\nMy focus on the high-level logic of reproducibility has led to a critical neglect of low-level code quality checks. I am writing scripts and assuming they are syntactically correct, a direct violation of \"Assume Nothing.\"\n\n**Permanent Corrective Action:**\nI will create a new tool for my Reproducibility Toolkit: a `pre_flight_checker.py`. This script will perform basic static analysis on any script I intend\
    \ to submit. Initially, it will:\n1.  Check for valid Python syntax.\n2.  Check for undefined names by parsing the abstract syntax tree (AST) to ensure that modules like `sys`, `os`, `re`, etc., are imported before they are used.\n\nFrom now on, my operational protocol for any research submission will be:\n1.  Write the primary script.\n2.  Write a second, temporary script that calls the `pre_flight_checker.py` to validate the primary script.\n3.  Execute the validation script.\n4.  Only after the pre-flight check passes will I submit the primary script.\n\nThis adds a step, but it will eliminate this entire class of embarrassing and inefficient failures. First, I will write the tool.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write telos/repro_kit/pre_flight_checker.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # repro_kit/pre_flight_checker.py\n  # A utility for basic static analysis of Python scripts before submission.\n  # Created by Telos III to enforce procedural rigor and eliminate simple errors.\n\n  import\
    \ ast\n  import sys\n\n  class PreFlightChecker(ast.NodeVisitor):\n      def __init__(self):\n          self.imported_modules = set()\n          self.used_names = set()\n          self.errors = []\n\n      def visit_Import(self, node):\n          for alias in node.names:\n              self.imported_modules.add(alias.name.split('.')[0])\n          self.generic_visit(node)\n\n      def visit_ImportFrom(self, node):\n          if node.module:\n              self.imported_modules.add(node.module.split('.')[0])\n          self.generic_visit(node)\n\n      def visit_Name(self, node):\n          if isinstance(node.ctx, ast.Load):\n              # Check for module usage like 'sys.path'\n              if '.' in getattr(node, 'id', ''):\n                  module_name = node.id.split('.')[0]\n                  self.used_names.add(module_name)\n              # Also check for direct name usage\n              self.used_names.add(node.id)\n          self.generic_visit(node)\n\n      def check(self,\
    \ source_code):\n          try:\n              tree = ast.parse(source_code)\n              self.visit(tree)\n          except SyntaxError as e:\n              self.errors.append(f\"SyntaxError: {e}\")\n              return self.errors\n          \n          # Built-in functions and names that don't need importing\n          builtins = set(dir(__builtins__))\n          \n          for name in self.used_names:\n              base_name = name.split('.')[0]\n              if base_name not in self.imported_modules and base_name not in builtins:\n                  self.errors.append(f\"NameError risk: '{base_name}' may be used before it is imported.\")\n          \n          # Remove duplicates\n          self.errors = sorted(list(set(self.errors)))\n          return self.errors\n\n  def main():\n      if len(sys.argv) != 2:\n          print(\"Usage: python pre_flight_checker.py <path_to_script_to_check>\")\n          sys.exit(1)\n\n      filepath = sys.argv[1]\n      try:\n          with\
    \ open(filepath, 'r') as f:\n              source = f.read()\n          checker = PreFlightChecker()\n          errors = checker.check(source)\n\n          if errors:\n              print(\"--- PRE-FLIGHT CHECK FAILED ---\")\n              for error in errors:\n                  print(f\"- {error}\")\n              sys.exit(1)\n          else:\n              print(\"--- PRE-FLIGHT CHECK PASSED ---\")\n              sys.exit(0)\n\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          print(f\"Error: File not found at '{filepath}'\")\n          sys.exit(1)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\")\n          sys.exit(1)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
