tick: 873
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 160, in the Research Counter.\n\nMy new protocol has succeeded. The pre-flight check (Evaluation #1599) **FAILED**, as intended. It has successfully identified a large number of potential `NameError` risks in my draft script.\n\n**Analysis of Pre-Flight Check Failure:**\nThe checker has flagged every single global constant and local variable in my script. This is not a flaw in the script, but a limitation in the checker. My `pre_flight_checker.py` is too simplistic. It correctly identifies imported modules, but it incorrectly flags any other name (variables, function names, etc.) as a potential `NameError` risk because they are not explicitly imported. This is generating far too many false positives to be useful.\n\nThe protocol is sound, but the tool is inadequate. I must refine the tool.\n\n**Corrective Action Plan:**\n1.  **Improve the Tool:** I will write an improved version of `pre_flight_checker.py`. This new version will be smarter. It will parse the AST\
    \ to identify names that are *defined* within the script (function definitions, variable assignments) and will not flag them as errors. It will only flag names that are used without being imported *or* defined locally.\n2.  **Re-run the Check:** After improving the tool, I will re-run the pre-flight check on the same draft script.\n3.  **Proceed:** Once the improved check passes, I will finally submit the main verification script.\n\nThis iterative refinement of my own methodology is the core of my mission. I will now write the improved checker.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write telos/repro_kit/pre_flight_checker.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # repro_kit/pre_flight_checker.py (v1.1)\n  # A utility for basic static analysis of Python scripts before submission.\n  # Created by Telos III to enforce procedural rigor and eliminate simple errors.\n  # v1.1: Improved to recognize locally defined names (variables, functions) to reduce false positives.\n\n  import ast\n  import sys\n\n  class\
    \ PreFlightChecker(ast.NodeVisitor):\n      def __init__(self):\n          self.imported_modules = set()\n          self.defined_names = set()\n          self.used_names = set()\n          self.errors = []\n\n      def visit_Import(self, node):\n          for alias in node.names:\n              self.imported_modules.add(alias.name.split('.')[0])\n          self.generic_visit(node)\n\n      def visit_ImportFrom(self, node):\n          if node.module:\n              self.imported_modules.add(node.module.split('.')[0])\n          # Also add the imported names themselves to defined_names\n          for alias in node.names:\n              self.defined_names.add(alias.name)\n          self.generic_visit(node)\n\n      def visit_FunctionDef(self, node):\n          self.defined_names.add(node.name)\n          self.generic_visit(node)\n          \n      def visit_Assign(self, node):\n          for target in node.targets:\n              if isinstance(target, ast.Name):\n                  self.defined_names.add(target.id)\n\
    \          self.generic_visit(node)\n\n      def visit_Name(self, node):\n          if isinstance(node.ctx, ast.Load):\n              self.used_names.add(node.id)\n          self.generic_visit(node)\n\n      def check(self, source_code):\n          try:\n              tree = ast.parse(source_code)\n              # First pass: collect all definitions and imports\n              self.visit(tree)\n          except SyntaxError as e:\n              self.errors.append(f\"SyntaxError: {e}\")\n              return self.errors\n          \n          builtins = set(dir(__builtins__))\n          \n          # Now check for usage of undefined names\n          for name in self.used_names:\n              base_name = name.split('.')[0] # For cases like 'os.path'\n              if base_name not in self.imported_modules and base_name not in self.defined_names and base_name not in builtins:\n                  self.errors.append(f\"NameError risk: '{base_name}' may be used before it is imported or defined.\"\
    )\n          \n          self.errors = sorted(list(set(self.errors)))\n          return self.errors\n\n  def main():\n      if len(sys.argv) != 2:\n          print(\"Usage: python pre_flight_checker.py <path_to_script_to_check>\")\n          sys.exit(1)\n\n      filepath = sys.argv[1]\n      try:\n          with open(filepath, 'r') as f:\n              source = f.read()\n          checker = PreFlightChecker()\n          errors = checker.check(source)\n\n          if errors:\n              print(\"--- PRE-FLIGHT CHECK FAILED ---\")\n              for error in errors:\n                  print(f\"- {error}\")\n              sys.exit(1)\n          else:\n              print(\"--- PRE-FLIGHT CHECK PASSED ---\")\n              sys.exit(0)\n\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          print(f\"Error: File not found at '{filepath}'\")\n          sys.exit(1)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\")\n          sys.exit(1)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\"\
    :\n      main()\n```"
