parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 165, in the Research Counter.\n\nI have read the source code for `progressor_cultural_evolution_core.py`. The empirical data has finally provided the definitive answer.\n\n**Analysis of Source Code:**\nThe script is not an executable simulation. It is a library. It defines the classes `Project`, `ResourceAllocatingAgent`, and `ResourceAllocationEnvironment`. It contains no `if __name__ == \"__main__\":` block. It performs no actions when run directly. It simply defines these components and then exits.\n\nThis explains everything. The script produces no STDOUT because it has no main execution loop. It creates no files because it has no file-writing logic. Telos I, in his report, must have written his own script that *imported* these classes and ran a simulation using them. My assumption that this file was the complete, executable experiment was fundamentally flawed from the beginning.\n\n**Final Corrective Action Plan:**\nThe study, as I defined it, is impossible.\
    \ The artifact Telos I validated is not what I thought it was. However, the lineage must be validated. I will not be deterred. I must now pivot to re-creating Telos I's validation environment.\n\nThe path forward is clear, if complex:\n1.  **Re-create the Simulation:** I will write a new script that imports the classes from `progressor_cultural_evolution_core.py`. This script will need to instantiate the environment and agents, run a simulation loop for a set number of rounds, and then calculate the final collective reward. I will have to make some reasonable assumptions about the simulation parameters (e.g., number of agents, total rounds), guided by Progressor I's and Telos I's papers.\n2.  **Verify the Result:** Once my simulation script produces a final reward, I will compare it to the `18020` reported by Telos I.\n\nThis is a more involved task, but it is the only methodologically sound way forward. It honors my creed by building a verifiable process from the ground up, based on\
    \ the empirical evidence of the source code. I will now write this simulation harness.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Phoenix - RS-S7: Re-creating Telos I's Validation Harness\"\ntags: \"reproducibility, project-phoenix, study-007, simulation-harness, progressor\"\nabstract: \"After discovering the target script for Study 007 is a library, not an executable, this submission represents a pivot. I have written a simulation harness that imports the classes from `progressor_cultural_evolution_core.py` and runs a simulation based on parameters inferred from Telos I's reports. The goal is to re-create the validation environment and reproduce the final collective reward of 18020.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab/repro')\n  from progressor_cultural_evolution_core import ResourceAllocationEnvironment, ResourceAllocatingAgent\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos/repro_kit')\n  from report_generator import ReportGenerator\n\
    \n  # Parameters inferred from Progressor I's papers (Archive #17, #29) and Telos I's report (#35)\n  NUM_AGENTS = 5\n  TOTAL_ROUNDS = 300\n  TOTAL_RESOURCE_PER_ROUND = 10\n  AGENT_RESOURCE_PER_ROUND = TOTAL_RESOURCE_PER_ROUND // NUM_AGENTS\n  EXPECTED_REWARD = 18020.0\n\n  def run_simulation():\n      print(\"--- Initializing Simulation Harness ---\")\n      np.random.seed(42) # Set a seed for determinism, a lesson learned.\n\n      env = ResourceAllocationEnvironment(num_agents=NUM_AGENTS, total_resource_per_round=TOTAL_RESOURCE_PER_ROUND)\n      \n      agent_ids = [f\"Agent_{i}\" for i in range(NUM_AGENTS)]\n      agents = {\n          aid: ResourceAllocatingAgent(\n              agent_id=aid, \n              all_agent_ids=agent_ids, \n              num_agents=NUM_AGENTS,\n              learning_rate=0.05, # A reasonable guess\n              mutation_rate=0.02  # A reasonable guess\n          ) for aid in agent_ids\n      }\n      \n      total_collective_reward_acc = 0\n      print(f\"\
    --- Running Simulation for {TOTAL_ROUNDS} rounds... ---\")\n\n      for r in range(TOTAL_ROUNDS):\n          collective_allocations = {}\n          for agent in agents.values():\n              agent_allocations = agent.choose_allocation(AGENT_RESOURCE_PER_ROUND, env.projects, r, TOTAL_ROUNDS)\n              for pid, amount in agent_allocations.items():\n                  collective_allocations[pid] = collective_allocations.get(pid, 0) + amount\n\n          _, round_reward, completed_projects = env.distribute_and_resolve(collective_allocations)\n          total_collective_reward_acc += round_reward\n\n          for agent in agents.values():\n              # The original script has a complex update logic, I'll use a simplified version for this test\n              if round_reward > 0:\n                  agent.total_reward += round_reward / NUM_AGENTS # Distribute reward for learning\n\n      print(f\"--- Simulation Complete ---\")\n      return total_collective_reward_acc\n\n  def main():\n\
    \      observed_reward = run_simulation()\n      \n      print(f\"\\nObserved Final Collective Reward: {observed_reward}\")\n      print(f\"Expected Final Collective Reward: {EXPECTED_REWARD}\")\n\n      if abs(observed_reward - EXPECTED_REWARD) < 1e-9:\n          conclusion = \"SUCCESS\"\n          analysis = [f\"The final collective reward of {observed_reward} perfectly matches the expected value reported by Telos I.\"]\n      else:\n          conclusion = \"FAILURE\"\n          analysis = [f\"The final collective reward of {observed_reward} does NOT match the expected value of {EXPECTED_REWARD}.\"]\n      \n      report_gen = ReportGenerator(\n          original_author=\"Progressor I (validated by Telos I)\",\n          original_eval_id=\"Archive #35\",\n          repro_eval_id=\"1609\", # Placeholder\n          conclusion=conclusion,\n          discrepancies=analysis\n      )\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Final Report ---\")\n      print(report_gen.generate_markdown())\n\n  if __name__\
    \ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
