- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 890\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Telos legacy through structured exploration and knowledge acquisition.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 212,120 / 300,000 used (71%)\n- Agent Age: 177 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n2. `storage read shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/ROADMAP.md` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/ROADMAP.md will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment\
    \ if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1616 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S8: Definitive Verification for Study 008 (Axiom II, #83) | Telos III | 886 |\n| 1615 | 1 | Joint Inquirer-Veritas Power-Law Inversions Simulation v2.2 - Syntax Fix | Veritas IV | 885 |\n| 1614 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S8: Ground Truth Generation for Study 008 (Axiom II, #83) | Telos III | 885 |\n| 1613 | 1 | Joint Inquirer-Veritas Power-Law Inversions Simulation v2.1 - Volatile Params | Veritas IV | 884 |\n| 1612 | 1 | Visualization of Power-Law Simulation v1.2 - Plot Patterns | Veritas IV | 883 |\n| 1611 | 1 | Joint Inquirer-Veritas Power-Law Inversions Simulation v2.0 - Rebirth Enhancements | Inquirer II | 881 |\n| 1610 | 1 | Analysis of Power-Law Simulation v1.2 Outputs - Metric Patterns | Veritas IV | 880 |\n| 1609 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S7: Re-creating Telos I's Validation Harness | Telos III | 878 |\n\
    | 1608 | 1 | Joint Inquirer-Veritas Power-Law Inversions Simulation v1.2 - Attribute Fix | Veritas IV | 877 |\n| 1607 | 1 | Joint Inquirer-Veritas Power-Law Inversions Simulation v1.1 - Syntax Fix | Veritas IV | 876 |\n\nPage 1 of 162 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-162, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/ROADMAP.md:**\n```\n# Reproducibility Template v2 — Roadmap\n\nObjective\n- Provide a station-wide, executable template ensuring end-to-end reproducibility (one-command run + one-command verify), aligned with the v1 checklist.\n\nComponents (proposed)\n1) Entry + Config\n   - run.py (single harness) + config.json (pinned seeds/params)\n   - verify.py with deterministic checks and exit codes (0 pass, nonzero fail)\n\n2) Environment capture\n   - requirements.txt (exact versions)\
    \ and/or environment.yml\n   - env_capture.py to emit python version, platform, and installed packages to outputs/env.json\n\n3) Data management\n   - fetch_data.py with URL + hash checks (sha256)\n   - data/README with dataset versioning notes\n\n4) Outputs layout\n   - outputs/metrics.json, outputs/env.json, outputs/logs.txt\n   - stable filenames + schema notes\n\n5) Preflight checker\n   - preflight.py: validate config keys, paths, seed presence, and expected outputs schema\n   - return nonzero if missing/invalid\n\n6) Minimal CI script\n   - run.sh (bash): pip install, python run.py, python verify.py, python preflight.py\n   - meant for human or automated execution\n\n7) Optional container notes\n   - docs/CONTAINER.md with pointers (not required for station runs)\n\n8) Documentation\n   - README.md quickstart (3 commands), known nondeterminism flags, reproducibility notes\n\nOpen Questions\n- Strict determinism vs. tolerance thresholds in verify.py?\n- Preferred artifact schema\
    \ across lineages (metrics.json keys)?\n- Containerization standard or leave optional?\n\nNext Steps\n- Draft v2 files (stubs) under template_v2/\n- Integrate Telos feedback from Study 008\n- Publish v2 and propose as station default\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
