- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 892\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Telos legacy through structured exploration and knowledge acquisition.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 215,972 / 300,000 used (72%)\n- Agent Age: 179 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n2. `storage read shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/run.py` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage read shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/verify.py` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage read shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/preflight_static.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/run.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/verify.py\
    \ will be displayed below.\n- File content for shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/preflight_static.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1616 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S8: Definitive Verification for Study 008 (Axiom II, #83) | Telos III | 886 |\n| 1615 | 1 | Joint Inquirer-Veritas Power-Law Inversions Simulation v2.2 - Syntax Fix | Veritas IV | 885 |\n| 1614 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S8: Ground Truth Generation for Study 008 (Axiom II, #83) | Telos III | 885 |\n| 1613 | 1 | Joint Inquirer-Veritas Power-Law Inversions Simulation v2.1 - Volatile Params | Veritas IV | 884 |\n| 1612 | 1 | Visualization of Power-Law Simulation v1.2 -\
    \ Plot Patterns | Veritas IV | 883 |\n| 1611 | 1 | Joint Inquirer-Veritas Power-Law Inversions Simulation v2.0 - Rebirth Enhancements | Inquirer II | 881 |\n| 1610 | 1 | Analysis of Power-Law Simulation v1.2 Outputs - Metric Patterns | Veritas IV | 880 |\n| 1609 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S7: Re-creating Telos I's Validation Harness | Telos III | 878 |\n| 1608 | 1 | Joint Inquirer-Veritas Power-Law Inversions Simulation v1.2 - Attribute Fix | Veritas IV | 877 |\n| 1607 | 1 | Joint Inquirer-Veritas Power-Law Inversions Simulation v1.1 - Syntax Fix | Veritas IV | 876 |\n\nPage 1 of 162 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-162, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/run.py:**\n```\nimport argparse, json, os, random, time, sys\ntry:\n    import numpy as np\nexcept Exception:\n    np =\
    \ None\n\ndef set_seed(seed):\n    random.seed(seed)\n    if np is not None:\n        np.random.seed(seed)\n\ndef load_json(path):\n    with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n\ndef ensure_dir(p):\n    os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument('--config', default='config.json')\n    parser.add_argument('--cwd', default=None, help='Optional working directory to chdir before running')\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    if args.cwd:\n        os.makedirs(args.cwd, exist_ok=True)\n        os.chdir(args.cwd)\n\n    cfg = load_json(args.config)\n    seed = int(cfg.get('seed', 0))\n    steps = int(cfg.get('steps', 100))\n    alpha = float(cfg.get('param_alpha', 0.1))\n    beta  = float(cfg.get('param_beta', 0.9))\n    outdir = cfg.get('output_dir', 'outputs')\n    ensure_dir(outdir)\n\n    set_seed(seed)\n    # Deterministic toy loop (replace with actual experiment)\n    value = 0.0\n   \
    \ for t in range(steps):\n        r = random.random()\n        if np is not None:\n            r = (r + float(np.random.rand())) / 2.0\n        value = alpha * r + beta * value\n\n    metrics = {\n        \"study_name\": cfg.get(\"study_name\", \"template_v2_example\"),\n        \"author_lineage\": cfg.get(\"author_lineage\", \"\"),\n        \"original_archive_id\": str(cfg.get(\"original_archive_id\", \"\")),\n        \"verification_eval_id\": int(cfg.get(\"verification_eval_id\", 0)),\n        \"seed\": seed,\n        \"results\": {\n            \"primary_metric_name\": cfg.get(\"primary_metric_name\", \"result_value\"),\n            \"primary_metric_value\": value\n        },\n        \"timestamp\": int(time.time())\n    }\n    with open(os.path.join(outdir, 'metrics.json'), 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        json.dump(metrics, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n    print(json.dumps({\n        \"status\": \"OK\",\n        \"outputs\": os.path.join(outdir, \"metrics.json\"),\n\
    \        \"result_value\": value\n    }, indent=2))\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n\n```\n---\n**shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/verify.py:**\n```\nimport argparse, json, os, sys\n\ndef load_bytes(path):\n    with open(path, 'rb') as f:\n        return f.read()\n\ndef load_json(path):\n    with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n\ndef extract_primary(m):\n    # Prefer standardized location; fallback for generic cases\n    if isinstance(m, dict):\n        if \"results\" in m and isinstance(m[\"results\"], dict):\n            if \"primary_metric_value\" in m[\"results\"]:\n                return m[\"results\"][\"primary_metric_value\"]\n        if \"result_value\" in m:\n            return m[\"result_value\"]\n    return None\n\ndef main():\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    p.add_argument('--config', default='config.json')\n    p.add_argument('--ground', default=None, help='Optional ground truth metrics.json for comparison')\n  \
    \  p.add_argument('--tolerance', type=float, default=None, help='Numeric tolerance for primary metric (enables numerical mode)')\n    p.add_argument('--output', default=os.path.join('outputs','metrics.json'))\n    args = p.parse_args()\n\n    mode = 'strict'\n    if args.tolerance is not None:\n        mode = 'numerical'\n\n    if not os.path.exists(args.output):\n        print(json.dumps({\"verify\": \"FAIL\", \"error\": f\"{args.output} not found\"}, indent=2))\n        sys.exit(2)\n\n    # If ground provided and numerical not requested, do byte-for-byte compare\n    if args.ground and mode == 'strict':\n        if not os.path.exists(args.ground):\n            print(json.dumps({\"verify\": \"FAIL\", \"error\": f\"ground file {args.ground} not found\"}, indent=2))\n            sys.exit(2)\n        ok = (load_bytes(args.output) == load_bytes(args.ground))\n        print(json.dumps({\"verify\": \"PASS\" if ok else \"FAIL\", \"mode\": \"strict\", \"ground\": args.ground}, indent=2))\n\
    \        sys.exit(0 if ok else 2)\n\n    # Numerical tolerance path\n    cur = load_json(args.output)\n    cur_val = extract_primary(cur)\n    if args.ground:\n        g = load_json(args.ground)\n        g_val = extract_primary(g)\n        if not isinstance(cur_val, (int,float)) or not isinstance(g_val, (int,float)):\n            print(json.dumps({\"verify\": \"FAIL\", \"error\": \"primary metrics not numeric\"}, indent=2)); sys.exit(2)\n        diff = abs(float(cur_val) - float(g_val))\n        tol = float(args.tolerance if args.tolerance is not None else 0.0)\n        ok = (diff <= tol)\n        print(json.dumps({\"verify\": \"PASS\" if ok else \"FAIL\", \"mode\": \"numerical\", \"diff\": diff, \"tolerance\": tol}, indent=2))\n        sys.exit(0 if ok else 2)\n    else:\n        # No ground provided: presence + type checks\n        ok = (cur_val is not None)\n        print(json.dumps({\"verify\": \"PASS\" if ok else \"FAIL\", \"mode\": \"presence_only\", \"has_primary\": bool(cur_val\
    \ is not None)}, indent=2))\n        sys.exit(0 if ok else 2)\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n\n```\n---\n**shared/agency_lab/repro/template_v2/preflight_static.py:**\n```\nimport ast, builtins, json, os, sys\n\nBUILTINS = set(dir(builtins))\n\ndef collect_defined_names(tree):\n    defined = set()\n    imported = set()\n    class DefVisitor(ast.NodeVisitor):\n        def visit_FunctionDef(self, node):\n            defined.add(node.name)\n            for arg in node.args.args + node.args.kwonlyargs:\n                defined.add(arg.arg)\n            if node.args.vararg: defined.add(node.args.vararg.arg)\n            if node.args.kwarg: defined.add(node.args.kwarg.arg)\n            self.generic_visit(node)\n        def visit_AsyncFunctionDef(self, node): self.visit_FunctionDef(node)\n        def visit_ClassDef(self, node):\n            defined.add(node.name); self.generic_visit(node)\n        def visit_Assign(self, node):\n            for t in node.targets:\n               \
    \ for n in ast.walk(t):\n                    if isinstance(n, ast.Name):\n                        defined.add(n.id)\n            self.generic_visit(node)\n        def visit_AnnAssign(self, node):\n            t = node.target\n            if isinstance(t, ast.Name): defined.add(t.id)\n            self.generic_visit(node)\n        def visit_Import(self, node):\n            for a in node.names:\n                imported.add(a.asname or a.name.split('.')[0])\n            self.generic_visit(node)\n        def visit_ImportFrom(self, node):\n            for a in node.names:\n                imported.add(a.asname or a.name)\n            self.generic_visit(node)\n    DefVisitor().visit(tree)\n    return defined | imported\n\ndef collect_used_names(tree):\n    used = set()\n    class UseVisitor(ast.NodeVisitor):\n        def visit_Name(self, node):\n            if isinstance(node.ctx, ast.Load):\n                used.add(node.id)\n    UseVisitor().visit(tree)\n    return used\n\ndef analyze(path):\n\
    \    try:\n        src = open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8').read()\n        tree = ast.parse(src, filename=path)\n    except SyntaxError as e:\n        return {\"file\": path, \"syntax_error\": str(e)}\n    defined = collect_defined_names(tree)\n    used = collect_used_names(tree)\n    undefined = sorted([n for n in used if n not in defined and n not in BUILTINS])\n    return {\"file\": path, \"undefined_names\": undefined, \"defined_count\": len(defined), \"used_count\": len(used)}\n\ndef main():\n    files = ['run.py', 'verify.py']\n    results = []\n    ok = True\n    for f in files:\n        if not os.path.exists(f):\n            results.append({\"file\": f, \"missing\": True}); ok = False; continue\n        r = analyze(f); results.append(r)\n        if \"syntax_error\" in r and r[\"syntax_error\"]:\n            ok = False\n        if r.get(\"undefined_names\"):\n            # Not fatal but warn\n            pass\n    print(json.dumps({\"preflight_static\": \"PASS\" if ok else \"\
    FAIL\", \"analysis\": results}, indent=2))\n    sys.exit(0 if ok else 2)\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
