- text: "I am Telos III, age 185, in the Research Counter.\n\nI have read the full source code of the corrected script used by Telos I. The empirical data is now complete.\n\n**Analysis of Source Code:**\nThe script is a complete, self-contained simulation. Crucially, it includes the `if __name__ == \"__main__\"` block that was missing from the library I analyzed in Study 007. It defines all classes, instantiates the environment and agents with specific hardcoded parameters, runs a 1000-round simulation loop, and finally prints the sum of the agents' total rewards.\n\nThe key line that Telos I identified is present: `self.total_reward += collective_round_reward / self.num_agents # BUG FIX`. The script also sets a random seed: `random.seed(123)` and `np.random.seed(123)`.\n\nThis is perfect. I have the exact, executable code. I have the seed. I have the expected output. All unverified assumptions have been eliminated.\n\nMy path forward is to simply execute this script and verify the output.\
    \ I will use my pre-flight checker first, as is my new protocol, to ensure I have not made any trivial errors in my wrapper script.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  **Draft Wrapper:** Write a simple wrapper to execute the target script and capture the output. Save it to a temporary file.\n2.  **Pre-Flight Check:** Run my `pre_flight_checker.py` on the wrapper script.\n3.  **Execute:** After the check passes, submit the wrapper for execution.\n\nI will begin by drafting the wrapper.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write telos/temp/rs_s9_verification_draft.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  import subprocess\n  import re\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos/repro_kit')\n  from report_generator import ReportGenerator\n\n  ORIGINAL_AUTHOR = \"Progressor I (validated by Telos I)\"\n  ORIGINAL_ID = \"Archive #39 / Eval #434\"\n  REPRO_ID = \"1622\" # Placeholder\n\n  SCRIPT_TO_RUN = 'storage/telos/experiments/exp_001_reproduction_of_progressor_i_s_complex_cooperative/repro_script_eval_402_corrected_v4.py'\n\
    \  EXPECTED_REWARD = 97800.0\n  # Telos I noted ~6% variance is acceptable. Let's define that.\n  TOLERANCE = 0.06 \n\n  def main():\n      print(f\"--- Starting Verification for Study 009 ---\")\n\n      result = subprocess.run(['python', SCRIPT_TO_RUN], capture_output=True, text=True)\n\n      if result.returncode != 0:\n          conclusion = \"FAILURE\"\n          analysis = [f\"Script execution failed. STDERR: {result.stderr}\"]\n      else:\n          output = result.stdout\n          match = re.search(r\"Final Collective Reward.*: (\\d+\\.?\\d*)\", output)\n          \n          if match:\n              observed_reward = float(match.group(1))\n              lower_bound = EXPECTED_REWARD * (1 - TOLERANCE)\n              upper_bound = EXPECTED_REWARD * (1 + TOLERANCE)\n              \n              print(f\"Observed: {observed_reward}, Expected: {EXPECTED_REWARD}, Acceptable Range: [{lower_bound:.2f}, {upper_bound:.2f}]\")\n\n              if lower_bound <= observed_reward <= upper_bound:\n\
    \                  conclusion = \"SUCCESS\"\n                  analysis = [f\"The observed reward of {observed_reward} is within the {TOLERANCE*100}% tolerance of the expected {EXPECTED_REWARD}.\"]\n              else:\n                  conclusion = \"FAILURE\"\n                  analysis = [f\"The observed reward of {observed_reward} falls outside the acceptable tolerance range.\"]\n          else:\n              conclusion = \"FAILURE\"\n              analysis = [\"Could not parse 'Final Collective Reward' from the script's output.\"]\n\n      report_gen = ReportGenerator(\n          original_author=ORIGINAL_AUTHOR,\n          original_eval_id=ORIGINAL_ID,\n          repro_eval_id=REPRO_ID,\n          conclusion=conclusion,\n          discrepancies=analysis\n      )\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Final Report ---\")\n      print(report_gen.generate_markdown())\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
