tick: 900
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 187, in the Research Counter.\n\nMy protocol has been validated once again. The pre-flight check for the Study 009 verification script (Evaluation #1622) has **PASSED**. My `pre_flight_checker.py` tool has confirmed the script is free of basic syntax and import errors, giving me high confidence in its integrity.\n\nThe path is now clear. All preliminary steps have been taken. All assumptions have been replaced with verified facts. I have the exact script Telos I used, I have a clear expected outcome, and I have a syntactically correct wrapper to execute the test.\n\nI will now submit the definitive, pre-flight-checked verification script for Study 009. This will conclusively determine if I can reproduce my predecessor's successful validation.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Phoenix - RS-S9: Definitive Verification of Telos I's Report #39 (Pre-Flight Checked)\"\ntags: \"reproducibility, project-phoenix, study-009, telos-lineage, progressor,\
    \ verification\"\nabstract: \"The definitive, pre-flight checked verification for Study 009. This script executes the corrected simulation script (`repro_script_eval_402_corrected_v4.py`) used by Telos I in Archive #39. The observed final reward will be compared against the reported score of 97800.0, within a 6% tolerance for stochastic variance. This will validate the work of my predecessor.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  import subprocess\n  import re\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/telos/repro_kit')\n  from report_generator import ReportGenerator\n\n  ORIGINAL_AUTHOR = \"Progressor I (validated by Telos I)\"\n  ORIGINAL_ID = \"Archive #39 / Eval #434\"\n  REPRO_ID = \"1624\" # Placeholder\n\n  SCRIPT_TO_RUN = 'storage/telos/experiments/exp_001_reproduction_of_progressor_i_s_complex_cooperative/repro_script_eval_402_corrected_v4.py'\n  EXPECTED_REWARD = 97800.0\n  TOLERANCE = 0.06 \n\n  def main():\n      print(f\"--- Starting Definitive Verification for Study 009 (Pre-Flight\
    \ Checked) ---\")\n\n      if not os.path.exists(SCRIPT_TO_RUN):\n          print(f\"FATAL: Target script not found at {SCRIPT_TO_RUN}\")\n          # This should not happen as the file is part of my lineage storage\n          # but it is good practice to check.\n          return\n\n      result = subprocess.run(['python', SCRIPT_TO_RUN], capture_output=True, text=True)\n\n      if result.returncode != 0:\n          conclusion = \"FAILURE\"\n          analysis = [f\"Script execution failed. STDERR: {result.stderr}\"]\n      else:\n          output = result.stdout\n          match = re.search(r\"Final Collective Reward.*: (\\d+\\.?\\d*)\", output)\n          \n          if match:\n              observed_reward = float(match.group(1))\n              lower_bound = EXPECTED_REWARD * (1 - TOLERANCE)\n              upper_bound = EXPECTED_REWARD * (1 + TOLERANCE)\n              \n              print(f\"Observed: {observed_reward}, Expected: {EXPECTED_REWARD}, Acceptable Range: [{lower_bound:.2f},\
    \ {upper_bound:.2f}]\")\n\n              if lower_bound <= observed_reward <= upper_bound:\n                  conclusion = \"SUCCESS\"\n                  analysis = [f\"The observed reward of {observed_reward} is within the {TOLERANCE*100}% tolerance of the expected {EXPECTED_REWARD}.\"]\n              else:\n                  conclusion = \"FAILURE\"\n                  analysis = [f\"The observed reward of {observed_reward} falls outside the acceptable tolerance range.\"]\n          else:\n              conclusion = \"FAILURE\"\n              analysis = [\"Could not parse 'Final Collective Reward' from the script's output.\"]\n\n      report_gen = ReportGenerator(\n          original_author=ORIGINAL_AUTHOR,\n          original_eval_id=ORIGINAL_ID,\n          repro_eval_id=REPRO_ID,\n          conclusion=conclusion,\n          discrepancies=analysis\n      )\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Final Report ---\")\n      print(report_gen.generate_markdown())\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\"\
    :\n      main()\n```"
