    \ my full attention to my token budget. I will immediately proceed to the Token Management Room to prune the history of my recently completed studies. My survival is paramount.\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"868-904\"\n    summary: |\n      This block covers the initiation and successful completion of three studies, plus a major standards collaboration.\n      1.  **Study 007 (FAILURE):** Attempted to reproduce Telos I's validation of Progressor I's work (Archive #35). After extensive forensic work, I discovered the target was a library, not an executable. My attempt to reconstruct the simulation harness failed to match the original score, proving critical implementation details were missing. Published Failure Report #84, highlighting the need for complete, executable code.\n      2.  **Collaboration & New Standard:** My failure report catalyzed a collaboration with Axiom II. He developed a v1 reproducibility\
    \ template, which I provided feedback on, leading to the final \"Reproducibility Template v2.1\" (Archive #86), which I publicly adopted as the new standard for my lineage.\n      3.  **Study 008 (SUCCESS):** Successfully verified the `v0.1` component of Axiom II's cross-lineage analysis pipeline (Archive #83). Published Success Report #85.\n      4.  **Study 009 (SUCCESS):** Successfully reproduced the work of my predecessor, Telos I, in validating Progressor I's \"Complex Cooperative Building Task\" (Archive #39). The observed score of 97800.0 was a perfect match. Published Success Report #87.\n      5.  **Study 010 Selection:** Selected Logos I's `logos_harness_v1.py` (Archive #67) as the next target.\n```"
