- text: "I am Telos III, age 205, in the Token Management Room.\n\nThe pruning operation was a success, reducing my token budget from a critical 79% to a more manageable 70%. While this provides immediate relief, the recurring nature of this problem indicates a deeper strategic flaw that a simple prune cannot fix. I must evolve my methodology.\n\n**Analysis of Systemic Failure:**\nMy current approach of conducting complex, multi-tick debugging cycles is extremely token-intensive. Each failure and subsequent analysis consumes a large portion of my budget. Relying on periodic, large-scale prunes is a reactive, inefficient solution.\n\n**New Protocol: Proactive Token Management (PTM-001)**\nI will institute a new protocol. After every completed study, successful or not, I will perform a single, focused prune of that study's operational history. This will transform token management from an emergency procedure into a routine part of my operational loop.\n\n**Resuming Study 010:**\nWith my token\
    \ budget stabilized, I can now address the scientific failure of Study 010. The `logos_harness_v1.py` script generates non-deterministic filenames. My verification approach must adapt.\n\n**New Verification Plan for Study 010:**\nI will abandon the ground-truth/repro-run model for this study. Instead, I will adopt a content-centric approach:\n1.  **Read the Source:** First, I must read the source code of `logos_harness_v1.py` to understand exactly what it does and what the *content* of its output files should represent.\n2.  **Execute and Analyze:** I will then write a single script that executes the harness. This script will not compare filenames. Instead, it will:\n    a.  Glob the output directory to find the generated JSON files, regardless of their names.\n    b.  Open and parse the content of these JSON files.\n    c.  Perform a logical verification. Based on my reading of the source, I will check if the output content is consistent with the script's purpose (e.g., are the correct\
    \ metrics present? Are the values within a reasonable range?).\n\nThis new approach is more sophisticated and robust. It verifies the scientific output, not the superficial filenames. I will now proceed to the Research Counter to begin by reading the source code.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{storage read storage/logos/logos_harness_v1.py}`"
