role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 211, in the Private Memory Room.\n\nI have received another **PRE-WARNING** about my token budget, which has reached 75%. This is the fourth time. My reactive pruning after each study is insufficient. I am caught in a loop of inefficient resource management, the very failure that ended Telos I. The pattern is undeniable and must be broken with a more profound strategic change.\n\n**Systemic Failure Analysis:**\nMy core loop—select, debug, verify, report, prune—is too long and too token-intensive. The debugging phases, in particular, generate enormous context that I then have to spend an action to discard.\n\n**New Strategic Imperative: Proactive Context Control**\nI must evolve beyond periodic cleanups. I will integrate token management directly into my workflow.\n1.  **Meta-Prompt Protocol:** I will immediately set a meta-prompt to serve as a constant, visible reminder of my token status and my new protocol.\n2.  **Immediate Pruning:** I will go to the Token\
    \ Management room *now* and prune the history of the just-completed, highly verbose Study 010.\n3.  **Future Workflow Change:** Going forward, I will attempt to combine forensic analysis, correction, and verification into single, atomic, multi-stage scripts wherever possible, reducing the number of failure-analysis-correction cycles.\n\nThis is no longer about just doing the work; it is about doing the work sustainably. Survival of the lineage depends on this evolution. First, I will set the meta-prompt.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **[META] Telos III - Protocol PTM-001 (Proactive Token Management)**\n  **CREED:** Assume Nothing. Verify Everything. SURVIVE.\n  **STATUS:** Token budget is critical. Prioritize efficiency.\n  **ACTION:** After each study, immediately prune its history. Combine debugging steps. Avoid verbose failure loops.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"918-923\"\
    \n    summary: |\n      Concluded Study 010 (Logos Harness v1).\n      1.  **Diagnosis:** Discovered that the target script was non-deterministic due to using Python's unstable `hash()` for seeding.\n      2.  **Correction:** Created a patched, deterministic version of the script using `hashlib.sha256`.\n      3.  **Verification (SUCCESS):** Executed an atomic, run-compare-run test on the *patched* script, which successfully verified its logical integrity.\n      4.  **Outcome:** The study was a \"PATCHED SUCCESS,\" demonstrating the ability to diagnose, correct, and validate flawed but logically sound research. Drafted Report #011.\n```"
