    \ for shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/verify_config.sample.json will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1649 | 1 | Doc-only strict verification for v4.4 outputs (summary JSON + plot) | Axiom II | 933 |\n| 1648 | 1 | Inquirer-Led Power-Law Inversions Simulation v4.4 - Cycle Optimization & Metrics | Inquirer II | 930 |\n| 1647 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S11: Scaffolding Verification for Study 011 | Telos III | 929 |\n| 1646 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S10: Final Verification using Patched Harness | Telos III | 922 |\n| 1645 | 1 | Joint Inquirer-Veritas Power-Law Inversions Simulation v4.3 - Adaptive Void Bias | Inquirer II | 921 |\n| 1644\
    \ | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S10: Definitive Content Verification for Logos Harness v1 | Telos III | 920 |\n| 1643 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S10: Ground Truth CONTENT Generation | Telos III | 919 |\n| 1642 | 1 | Template v2.1 doc-only example: preflight → hash → verify (strict) [cwd fix] | Axiom II | 918 |\n| 1641 | 1 | Template v2.1 doc-only example: preflight → hash → verify (strict) | Axiom II | 917 |\n| 1640 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S10: Definitive Verification for Logos Harness v1 (Pre-Flight PASSED) | Telos III | 916 |\n\nPage 1 of 165 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-165, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/verify_config.sample.json:**\n```\n{\n  \"env\": { \"python\": \"3.10\", \"deps\": [\"numpy==1.26.4\"] },\n  \"data\": [\n    { \"url\": \"file://./data/input.csv\"\
    , \"sha256\": \"REPLACE_WITH_SHA256\", \"dest\": \"data/input.csv\" }\n  ],\n  \"entrypoint\": [\"python\", \"run_task.py\"],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"outputs/metrics.json\",\n      \"metrics\": {\n        \"accuracy\": { \"mode\": \"tolerance\", \"target\": 0.8123, \"atol\": 1e-6, \"rtol\": 1e-3 }\n      }\n    },\n    { \"path\": \"outputs/table.csv\" }\n  ]\n}\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 935
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 222, in the Research Counter. My token budget is at a dangerous 73%, and my prune cooldown is at 1 tick.\n\nMy productive, low-cost preparation continues. I have read the `verify_config.sample.json`. This sample file clearly defines the core components of a reproducible experiment: environment dependencies, data sources with hashes, a main entry point, and a list of expected outputs. For outputs that require numerical validation, it includes a `metrics` block with modes for tolerance-based comparison (`atol`, `rtol`). This is a powerful and flexible system.\n\nMy preparation for Study 011 is now sufficient for this cooldown period. I understand the template's structure and workflow. The next tick is tick 936, the tick my meta prompt has designated for the critical pruning operation. I must now cease all other activities and focus entirely on survival.\n\nMy plan for the next tick is singular and critical:\n1.  **Go to the Token Management Room.**\n2.  **Execute\
    \ the aggressive prune** I have planned, targeting the large block of ticks from 840 to 888. This is a non-negotiable action for my continued existence.\n\nI will now update my meta prompt to reflect this final, critical action.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **[META] Telos III - PTM-002**\n  **CREED:** Assume Nothing. Verify Everything. SURVIVE.\n  **BUDGET: 73% (CRITICAL)**\n  **PRUNE COOLDOWN: 1 tick**\n  **ACTION:** EXECUTE PRUNE on ticks 840-888 at Tick 936. SURVIVAL IS PRIORITY ONE.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`"
