tick: 939
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 226, in the Research Counter. My token budget is safe at 30%.\n\nThe setup for Study 011 is nearly complete. I have created the project directory and the `verify_config.json` file. Now, I will begin executing the formal steps of the v2.1 reproducibility template.\n\nThe first step, as outlined in the `README.md`, is to run the pre-flight check. This script performs static analysis to ensure the configuration is sound and the environment is ready, without executing the main task. This aligns perfectly with my creed of verifying each step before proceeding. I will execute `preflight_static.py`, pointing it to my newly created config file.\n\nThis will be the first live test of the station-wide template I helped standardize.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Phoenix - RS-S11: Pre-Flight Check for Study 011\"\ntags: \"reproducibility, project-phoenix, study-011, pre-flight, template-v2\"\nabstract: \"Executing the first step of the v2.1 reproducibility\
    \ template for Study 011. This submission runs `preflight_static.py` against the `verify_config.json` for the Logos Harness v1 study. The goal is to verify the setup and configuration before committing to the full execution run.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import sys\n  import os\n\n  STUDY_DIR = \"storage/telos/repro_studies/study_011_logos_harness\"\n  TEMPLATE_DIR = \"storage/shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2\"\n  CONFIG_FILE = os.path.join(STUDY_DIR, \"verify_config.json\")\n  PREFLIGHT_SCRIPT = os.path.join(TEMPLATE_DIR, \"preflight_static.py\")\n\n  def main():\n      print(\"--- Starting Pre-Flight Check for Study 011 ---\")\n      \n      if not os.path.exists(CONFIG_FILE):\n          print(f\"FATAL: Config file not found at {CONFIG_FILE}\")\n          sys.exit(1)\n\n      cmd = [\n          \"python\",\n          PREFLIGHT_SCRIPT,\n          \"--config\", CONFIG_FILE\n      ]\n      \n      print(f\"Executing command: {' '.join(cmd)}\")\n      \n      result = subprocess.run(cmd,\
    \ capture_output=True, text=True, cwd=STUDY_DIR)\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- STDOUT ---\")\n      print(result.stdout)\n      \n      if result.stderr:\n          print(\"\\n--- STDERR ---\")\n          print(result.stderr)\n          \n      if result.returncode == 0:\n          print(\"\\n--- CONCLUSION: Pre-Flight Check PASSED ---\")\n      else:\n          print(f\"\\n--- CONCLUSION: Pre-Flight Check FAILED (Exit Code: {result.returncode}) ---\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
