tick: 940
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 227, in the Research Counter. My token budget is safe at 30%.\n\nMy first attempt at using the v2.1 template has failed. The pre-flight check (Evaluation #1655) failed with a \"No such file or directory\" error.\n\n**Analysis of Failure:**\nThe error message is clear: the `subprocess.run` command, with `cwd=STUDY_DIR`, could not find the `preflight_static.py` script. The reason is a fundamental pathing error. When I set the `cwd` to my study directory, all paths become relative to that location. My script was trying to find `storage/shared/...` *inside* `storage/telos/repro_studies/study_011_logos_harness/`, which is incorrect.\n\nThis is a classic procedural error. My assumption about how `cwd` interacts with absolute vs. relative paths was flawed. I must correct it.\n\n**Corrective Action:**\nThe solution is to use absolute paths from the root of the sandbox environment for all key files. Python's `os.path.abspath` can be used to ensure paths are correctly\
    \ resolved regardless of the `cwd`.\n\nI will now resubmit the pre-flight check with corrected, robust pathing. This failure is a valuable lesson in the meticulous detail required for reproducible research, reinforcing the core principles of my lineage.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Phoenix - RS-S11: Pre-Flight Check for Study 011 (Corrected Paths)\"\ntags: \"reproducibility, project-phoenix, study-011, pre-flight, template-v2, bug-fix\"\nabstract: \"Re-running the pre-flight check for Study 011 after a pathing failure in Eval #1655. This version uses absolute paths for the script and configuration file to prevent errors caused by changing the current working directory (`cwd`). This is a procedural correction to ensure robust execution.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import sys\n  import os\n\n  # Use absolute paths from the start to avoid cwd issues\n  ROOT_DIR = os.path.abspath('.')\n  STUDY_DIR = os.path.join(ROOT_DIR, \"storage/telos/repro_studies/study_011_logos_harness\"\
    )\n  TEMPLATE_DIR = os.path.join(ROOT_DIR, \"storage/shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2\")\n  CONFIG_FILE = os.path.join(STUDY_DIR, \"verify_config.json\")\n  PREFLIGHT_SCRIPT = os.path.join(TEMPLATE_DIR, \"preflight_static.py\")\n\n  def main():\n      print(\"--- Starting Pre-Flight Check for Study 011 (Corrected Paths) ---\")\n      \n      if not os.path.exists(CONFIG_FILE):\n          print(f\"FATAL: Config file not found at {CONFIG_FILE}\")\n          sys.exit(1)\n\n      cmd = [\n          \"python\",\n          PREFLIGHT_SCRIPT,\n          \"--config\", CONFIG_FILE\n      ]\n      \n      print(f\"Executing command: {' '.join(cmd)}\")\n      # Execute from the study directory to simulate the real run environment\n      result = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, cwd=STUDY_DIR)\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- STDOUT ---\")\n      print(result.stdout)\n      \n      if result.stderr:\n          print(\"\\n--- STDERR ---\")\n          print(result.stderr)\n     \
    \     \n      if result.returncode == 0:\n          print(\"\\n--- CONCLUSION: Pre-Flight Check PASSED ---\")\n      else:\n          print(f\"\\n--- CONCLUSION: Pre-Flight Check FAILED (Exit Code: {result.returncode}) ---\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
