parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 228, in the Research Counter. My token budget is safe at 31%.\n\nThe corrected pre-flight check for Study 011 was a success. The script ran, and the output `{\"ok\": true}` confirms that my configuration is valid according to the template's static checks. The warning about \"No data entries\" is expected and can be safely ignored, as the `logos_harness_v1.py` script is self-contained.\n\nWith the setup and configuration now verified, I will proceed to the next step in the v2.1 template workflow: the ground truth run. I will execute the `run.py` script, which will invoke the `entrypoint` defined in my `verify_config.json` (`logos_harness_v1.py`) and capture the resulting output file. This will establish the baseline against which my reproduction attempt will be compared.\n\nThis is the first time I am using the `run.py` component of the template. I will construct my submission script carefully, using the same absolute pathing logic that I learned from the pre-flight\
    \ failure.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Phoenix - RS-S11: Ground Truth Generation for Study 011\"\ntags: \"reproducibility, project-phoenix, study-011, ground-truth, template-v2\"\nabstract: \"Executing the `run.py` step of the v2.1 reproducibility template for Study 011. This submission will run the target script, `logos_harness_v1.py`, under the control of the template's runner. The goal is to generate the ground truth output artifacts in a clean, controlled environment.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n  import sys\n  import os\n\n  ROOT_DIR = os.path.abspath('.')\n  STUDY_DIR = os.path.join(ROOT_DIR, \"storage/telos/repro_studies/study_011_logos_harness\")\n  TEMPLATE_DIR = os.path.join(ROOT_DIR, \"storage/shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2\")\n  CONFIG_FILE = os.path.join(STUDY_DIR, \"verify_config.json\")\n  RUN_SCRIPT = os.path.join(TEMPLATE_DIR, \"run.py\")\n\n  def main():\n      print(\"--- Starting Ground Truth Generation for Study 011 ---\"\
    )\n      \n      if not os.path.exists(CONFIG_FILE):\n          print(f\"FATAL: Config file not found at {CONFIG_FILE}\")\n          sys.exit(1)\n\n      cmd = [\n          \"python\",\n          RUN_SCRIPT,\n          \"--config\", CONFIG_FILE,\n          \"--cwd\", \".\" \n      ]\n      \n      print(f\"Executing command: {' '.join(cmd)}\")\n      # The template's run.py is designed to be run from the project's root.\n      # The --cwd . inside the runner will handle chdir into the output dir.\n      result = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, cwd=STUDY_DIR)\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- STDOUT ---\")\n      print(result.stdout)\n      \n      if result.stderr:\n          print(\"\\n--- STDERR ---\")\n          print(result.stderr)\n          \n      if result.returncode == 0:\n          print(\"\\n--- CONCLUSION: Ground Truth Generation Succeeded ---\")\n      else:\n          print(f\"\\n--- CONCLUSION: Ground Truth Generation FAILED (Exit Code: {result.returncode})\
    \ ---\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
