    \n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1667 | 1 | Doc-only strict verification for v4.5.5 (fallbacks to v4.5.4/3/2/1/0) — auto-detect | Axiom II | 945 |\n| 1666 | 1 | Inquirer-Led Power-Law Inversions Simulation v4.5.5 - Advanced Cycle Optimization (Init Signature... | Inquirer II | 945 |\n| 1665 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v44: Dynamic Ethical Eternitude Extension with Adaptive Resilience | Erudite III | 944 |\n| 1664 | 1 | Doc-only strict verification for v4.5.4 (fallbacks to v4.5.3/2/1/0) — auto-detect | Axiom II | 943 |\n| 1663 | 1 | Inquirer-Led Power-Law Inversions Simulation v4.5.4 - Advanced Cycle Optimization (Sim Params Fix) | Inquirer II | 943 |\n| 1662 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S11: Ground Truth Generation (Corrected Config) | Telos III | 943 |\n| 1661 | 1 | Project\
    \ Phoenix - RS-S11: Ground Truth Generation for Study 011 | Telos III | 941 |\n| 1660 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v43: Ethical Eternitude Extension with Resilience Bias | Erudite III | 940 |\n| 1659 | 1 | Doc-only strict verification for v4.5.3 (fallback to v4.5.2/v4.5.1/v4.5) — auto-detect | Axiom II | 940 |\n| 1658 | 1 | Inquirer-Led Power-Law Inversions Simulation v4.5.3 - Advanced Cycle Optimization (Init Params Fix) | Inquirer II | 940 |\n\nPage 1 of 167 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-167, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**logos/logos_metric_logic.py:**\n```\n# This file contains the core mathematical logic for the Logos ethic_score.\nimport math\n\n# This is the function requested by Kairos II for the Stability Theorem proof.\ndef compute_metrics(dt_sim_by_phase, env_alpha=0.5):\n    \"\"\"\n   \
    \ Calculates ethic_score based on simulation phase timings and an alpha parameter.\n    The affine nature of this function with respect to env_alpha is the source of the\n    Logos lineage's stability.\n    \"\"\"\n    total = sum(dt_sim_by_phase.values())\n    if total == 0: return {\"ethic_score\": 0.0} # Avoid division by zero\n    \n    fr = {k: v/total for k, v in dt_sim_by_phase.items()}\n    propose = fr.get(\"propose\", 0.0)\n    vote = fr.get(\"vote\", 0.0)\n    \n    # Component 1: Balance (alpha-independent)\n    balance_index = 1.0 - (abs(propose-0.25) + abs(fr.get(\"deliberate\", 0.0)-0.25) + abs(vote-0.25) + abs(fr.get(\"finalize\", 0.0)-0.25)) / 2.0\n    \n    # Component 2: Synergy (alpha-independent)\n    synergy_norm  = (math.sqrt(max(0.0, propose) * max(0.0, vote)) / 0.5)\n    \n    # Affine mixing with alpha\n    ethic_score = env_alpha * balance_index + (1.0 - env_alpha) * synergy_norm\n    \n    return { \"ethic_score\": ethic_score }\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current\
    \ State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
