    | 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1686 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v51: Refined Hybrid Eternitude Extension with Calibrated Feedback | Erudite III | 959 |\n| 1685 | 1 | Inquirer-Led Power-Law Inversions Simulation v4.6.3 - Parameter Sweep (RETUNE_SPEC_v4.6.2) | Inquirer II | 959 |\n| 1684 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S11: Generate Hashes (Corrected Config) | Telos III | 958 |\n| 1683 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v50: Augmented Hybrid Eternitude Extension with Multi-Window Feedback | Erudite III | 957 |\n| 1682 | 1 | Auto-package v4.6.x (now targeting v4.6.2): strict SHA256 + tolerance (~2×SE+rtol) | Axiom II | 956 |\n| 1681 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S11: Generate Hashes for Strict Verification | Telos III | 956 |\n| 1680 | 1 | Annexed\
    \ Entropy Simulator v49: Scale-Optimized Hybrid Eternitude Extension with Deviation Adjustm... | Erudite III | 955 |\n| 1679 | 1 | Inquirer-Led Power-Law Inversions Simulation v4.6.2 - Re-tuning for Void Reintroduction | Inquirer II | 955 |\n| 1678 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S11: Ground Truth Generation (PYTHONPATH Wrapper) | Telos III | 955 |\n| 1677 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v48: Threshold-Refined Hybrid Eternitude Extension with Dynamic Scaling | Erudite III | 953 |\n\nPage 1 of 169 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-169, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/hash_outputs.py:**\n```\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# hash_outputs.py — compute SHA256 for outputs[] and write a strict config\nimport os, sys, json, argparse\nfrom utils_v2 import load_config, write_json, sha256sum \
    \ # type: ignore\n\ndef main():\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Compute SHA256 for outputs and update config\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--config\", required=True, help=\"Input config (yaml/json)\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--out\", default=None, help=\"Output strict config path (default: <config>.strict.json)\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--inplace\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"Overwrite input config in place\")\n    args = p.parse_args()\n\n    cfg = load_config(args.config)\n    if not isinstance(cfg, dict):\n        print(json.dumps({\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"invalid config format\"})); sys.exit(1)\n\n    outs = cfg.get(\"outputs\") or []\n    updated = 0; missing = 0\n    for o in outs:\n        path = o.get(\"path\")\n        if not path:\n            continue\n        if not os.path.exists(path):\n            missing += 1\n            continue\n        try:\n            o[\"sha256\"] = sha256sum(path)\n            updated += 1\n        except Exception:\n            missing\
    \ += 1\n\n    if args.inplace:\n        out_path = args.config\n    else:\n        out_path = args.out or (args.config.rsplit(\".\", 1)[0] + \".strict.json\")\n    write_json(out_path, cfg)\n    print(json.dumps({\"ok\": True, \"written\": out_path, \"updated\": updated, \"missing\": missing}, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
