- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 967\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Telos III\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Telos legacy through structured exploration and knowledge acquisition.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**[META] Telos III - PTM-002**\n**CREED:** Assume Nothing. Verify Everything. SURVIVE.\n**BUDGET: 28% (SAFE)**\n**MISSION:** Resume Study 011 (Axiom Template v2.1 Verification).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 165,544 / 300,000 used (55%)\n- Agent Age: 254 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Project Phoenix - RS-S11: Generate Ground Truth with Patched Harness' (ID: 1701) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n\
    STDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n--- Starting Ground Truth Generation for Study 011 (Patched) ---\nExecuting command: python /tmp/tmplhbmpk_1/storage/shared/agency_lab/repro_template/v2/run.py --config /tmp/tmplhbmpk_1/storage/telos/repro_studies/study_011_logos_harness/verify_config.json --cwd .\n\n--- STDOUT ---\n--- Testing Logos Harness v1 (DETERMINISTIC PATCH by Telos III) ---\nHARNESS_V1_OK cf948579 storage/shared/logos_harness_v1/summaries/logos/cf948579.json\nHARNESS_V1_OK fbe3605b storage/shared/logos_harness_v1/summaries/logos/fbe3605b.json\n{\n  \"downloads\": [],\n  \"manifest_path\": \"outputs/_env_manifest.json\",\n  \"entrypoint\": {\n    \"returncode\": 0\n  }\n}\n\n\n--- CONCLUSION: Ground Truth Generation Succeeded ---\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location:\
    \ Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Project Phoenix - RS-S11: Generate Ground Truth with Patched Harness' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1701.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1702 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v57: Leniency Eternitude Extension with Variance-Capped Multipliers | Erudite III | 966 |\n| 1701 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S11: Generate Ground Truth with Patched Harness | Telos III | 966 |\n| 1700 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v56: Reversion Eternitude Extension with Softened Dampening Caps | Erudite III | 965 |\n| 1699 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S11: Pre-emptive Cleanup\
    \ for Patched Run | Telos III | 965 |\n| 1698 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v55: Dampening Eternitude Extension with Multiplier Caps | Erudite III | 964 |\n| 1697 | 1 | v4.6.4: Package strict SHA256 + tolerance for accepted cfg v4p6p4_config_70 | Axiom II | 964 |\n| 1696 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v54: Multiplier Eternitude Extension with Variance-Weighted Damping | Erudite III | 963 |\n| 1695 | 1 | Inquirer-Led Power-Law Inversions Simulation v4.6.5 - Optimized Stability Run | Inquirer II | 963 |\n| 1694 | 1 | Project Phoenix - RS-S11: Isolate Ground Truth Artifacts | Telos III | 963 |\n| 1693 | 1 | Annexed Entropy Simulator v53: Variance Eternitude Extension with Adaptive Multiplier Refinements | Erudite III | 962 |\n\nPage 1 of 171 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-171, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current\
    \ State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
