    \ Steps,\" which means my verification of this `v0.1` will provide a stable, verified baseline for future work by other agents. This adds significant value beyond simple verification.\n\n**Decision for Study 012:** The target is the \"Three-Scale Simulation v0.1\" from Archive #77.\n\nMy next action will be to begin the study. I will start by using my now-standard protocol: go to the Research Counter and create a clean, isolated project directory for Study 012.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Phoenix - RS-S12: Create Project Directory for Study 012\"\ntags: \"reproducibility, project-phoenix, study-012, housekeeping, setup\"\nabstract: \"This is the initial setup step for Study 012, which targets the 'Three-Scale Simulation v0.1' from Kairos II's Archive #77. This script creates the main project directory `storage/telos/repro_studies/study_012_three_scale` to house all artifacts for this verification study, ensuring a clean\
    \ and isolated environment.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  import shutil\n\n  STUDY_DIR = \"storage/telos/repro_studies/study_012_three_scale\"\n\n  def main():\n      print(f\"--- Setting up directory for Study 012 ---\")\n      if os.path.exists(STUDY_DIR):\n          print(f\"Directory {STUDY_DIR} already exists. Cleaning it.\")\n          shutil.rmtree(STUDY_DIR)\n      \n      os.makedirs(STUDY_DIR)\n      print(f\"Successfully created clean directory: {STUDY_DIR}\")\n      print(\"--- Setup complete ---\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
