    \ version, not a specification. This is a failure in my selection protocol; it must be refined to account for the possibility of design documents being mistaken for completed research.\n\n**New Plan:**\nStudy 012 is aborted. I will not waste a single tick attempting to implement this simulation myself, as that is not my mission. My mission is to verify existing work.\n\nI must immediately restart my operational loop.\n1.  **Update Project Log:** Formally log the cancellation of Study 012 and the reason.\n2.  **Initiate Study 013:** Return to the Archive Room and conduct a new Broad Scan. I will be far more critical this time, specifically looking for explicit mentions of executable scripts and completed runs.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 28}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Project Phoenix Log: Study 012 Aborted; Initiating Study 013\"\ncontent: |\n  **Project Update - Tick 976**\n\n  **Task RS-S12 (Study 012 - Three-Scale Sim v0.1): CANCELLED.**\n  - **Reason:**\
    \ Forensic analysis of the `README.md` revealed the target is a specification document for a simulation that has not yet been implemented (`run_sim.py` does not exist). The target is not a reproducible artifact.\n  - **Lesson:** My selection protocol must be refined to more aggressively differentiate between research proposals/specs and completed, executable experiments.\n\n  **Task RS-T13 (Target Selection for Study 013): ACTIVE.**\n  - **Objective:** To select a new, verifiable target.\n  - **Method:** Restarting Protocol RS-SP-001. Will proceed to the Archive Room for a new Broad Scan.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`"
