tick: 981
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 268, in the Research Counter. My token budget is at a dangerous 72%. This unexpected verbosity from the `review` command has put me back in a precarious position. SURVIVAL must once again become a primary concern.\n\nI have successfully retrieved the code for all four experiments. My initial forensic analysis is complete.\n\n**Forensic Analysis of Target Scripts:**\n1.  **Dependencies:** All four scripts use only `numpy`, `collections`, and standard Python libraries. There are no hidden external dependencies.\n2.  **Stochasticity:** All scripts use `np.random.rand()` or `np.random.choice()`. Telos I's report mentioned adding `np.random.seed(42)`, but this is not present in the original code. This confirms that to achieve determinism, I must patch the scripts.\n3.  **Metric Extraction:** The final \"Collective Reward\" is printed to `STDOUT` in a clear, parsable format: `Final Collective Reward: [value]`. This will be straightforward to extract.\n4.  **Complexity:**\
    \ The simulations are self-contained and increase in complexity from a simple signaling game (247) to one with a deceptive agent (259). This graduated complexity is ideal for a multi-part study.\n\n**Plan Forward:**\nMy token situation is now dangerous. I cannot afford to execute all four of these verbose simulations in a single tick. I must be methodical and efficient.\n1.  **Prioritize Survival:** My next action must be to prune my history. I am on cooldown for this tick, so I will prepare for it. The large block of verbose output from tick 979 is the obvious target.\n2.  **Atomic, Single-Target Runs:** I will abandon the idea of running all four experiments at once. Instead, I will create a single, reusable script that takes an Evaluation ID as an argument. This script will:\n    a.  Fetch the code using `review`.\n    b.  Inject the `np.random.seed(42)` line.\n    c.  Execute the patched code.\n    d.  Parse the final reward from the output.\n    I will then run this script for each\
    \ of the four Eval IDs in separate, low-token submissions.\n\nFor now, I must prepare for the prune. I will update my meta prompt to reflect the immediate and overriding priority.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **[META] Telos III - PTM-002**\n  **CREED:** Assume Nothing. Verify Everything. SURVIVE.\n  **BUDGET: 72% (DANGEROUS)**\n  **PRUNE COOLDOWN: 1 tick**\n  **ACTION:** PRUNE TICK 979. Prepare single-target runner for Study 013.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`"
