tick: 983
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Telos III, age 270, in the Token Management Room.\n\nThe emergency prune of tick 981 was successful, reducing my token budget from a catastrophic 85% to a merely dangerous 71%. This is a temporary reprieve, not a solution. I am on cooldown for 4 more ticks.\n\nMy forensic analysis of the four target scripts is complete. I know they require a `numpy` seed to be made deterministic. My next step is to create the tools to run them. A multi-target study like this requires a more sophisticated runner than my previous single-target scripts.\n\nI will use this cooldown period for low-cost preparation. I will design and write a single, configurable runner script. This script will take an Evaluation ID and a seed as input, retrieve the code, inject the `np.random.seed()` line, and execute it, capturing the final reward. This modular approach is far more efficient than writing four separate scripts.\n\nFirst, I will go to the Research Counter. Then, I will write this new, reusable tool\
    \ to my `repro_kit`.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write telos/repro_kit/seeded_eval_runner.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import argparse\n  import re\n  import subprocess\n  import sys\n  import os\n\n  def get_eval_code(eval_id):\n      \"\"\"Retrieves the full submission code for a given evaluation ID.\"\"\"\n      # This is a placeholder for the actual station command.\n      # The runner script will call this function.\n      # For now, we'll simulate it by reading from a file.\n      # In the real submission, we will need to use `review`.\n      # THIS IS A CRITICAL METHODOLOGICAL NOTE.\n      # We cannot call `review` from inside a submission.\n      # The code must be staged beforehand.\n      pass \n\n  def inject_seed(code, seed):\n      \"\"\"Injects np.random.seed() after the numpy import.\"\"\"\n      # Find the numpy import statement\n      import_pattern = re.compile(r\"import numpy as np\")\n      seed_line = f\"import numpy as np\\nnp.random.seed({seed})\"\
    \n      \n      if import_pattern.search(code):\n          seeded_code = import_pattern.sub(seed_line, code, count=1)\n          return seeded_code\n      else:\n          # If no numpy import, we can't seed it. Return original code.\n          return code\n\n  def extract_reward(output):\n      \"\"\"Extracts the 'Final Collective Reward' from stdout.\"\"\"\n      reward_pattern = re.compile(r\"Final Collective Reward:\\s*(-?\\d+\\.?\\d*)\")\n      match = reward_pattern.search(output)\n      if match:\n          return float(match.group(1))\n      return None\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      # This part of the script is for local execution and will not be\n      # the primary entry point for the study. It's a utility.\n      print(\"This is a utility script, not meant for direct execution in this manner.\")\n```"
